        "What would make today count?": "Bug\xFCn\xFC ne de\u011Ferli k\u0131lar?",
        "Set decision": "Karar\u0131 belirle",
        "Three small habits": "\xDC\xE7 k\xFC\xE7\xFCk al\u0131\u015Fkanl\u0131k",
        "Add a habit": "Al\u0131\u015Fkanl\u0131k ekle",
        "See all {n}": "T\xFCm\xFCn\xFC g\xF6r ({n})",
        "Ready to claim": "Art\u0131k alabilirsin",
        "Pick your first dream": "\u0130lk hayalini se\xE7",
        "Daily rituals": "G\xFCnl\xFCk rit\xFCeller",
        "Meditate \xB7 check-in \xB7 reflection": "Meditasyon \xB7 yoklama \xB7 g\xFCn de\u011Ferlendirmesi",
        "The life you are building, and the one you get if nothing changes.": "Kurdu\u011Fun hayat ve hi\xE7bir \u015Fey de\u011Fi\u015Fmezse sana kalan hayat.",
        "{n}% of decisions building": "Kararlar\u0131n %{n}'i kuruyor",
        "What you keep accepting": "Kabul etmeye devam ettiklerin",
        "Not answered yet": "Hen\xFCz cevaplanmad\u0131",
        "What avoidance protects": "Ka\xE7\u0131nman\u0131n korudu\u011Fu \u015Fey",
        "An ordinary day in three years": "\xDC\xE7 y\u0131l sonra s\u0131radan bir g\xFCn",
        "Calm mornings, deep work, money that gives you room.": "Sakin sabahlar, derin \xE7al\u0131\u015Fma, sana alan a\xE7an para.",
        "What money lets you say no to": "Paran\u0131n hay\u0131r demeni sa\u011Flad\u0131\u011F\u0131 \u015Feyler",
        "Frantic schedules and work that does not fit.": "Tela\u015Fl\u0131 programlar ve sana uymayan i\u015Fler.",
        "Reread this once a week. It keeps your daily choices pointed the right way.": "Bunu haftada bir yeniden oku. G\xFCnl\xFCk se\xE7imlerini do\u011Fru y\xF6ne \xE7evirir.",
        "Dreams and bank": "Hayaller ve banka",
        "One bridge": "Bir k\xF6pr\xFC",
        "Unlimited bridges": "S\u0131n\u0131rs\u0131z k\xF6pr\xFC",
        "Custom dreams with images": "G\xF6rselli \xF6zel hayaller",
        "Seasons and badges": "Sezonlar ve rozetler",
        "High-resolution exports": "Y\xFCksek \xE7\xF6z\xFCn\xFCrl\xFCkl\xFC d\u0131\u015Fa aktar\u0131m",
        "Pro": "Pro",
        "One plan. Cancel any time.": "Tek plan. \u0130stedi\u011Fin zaman iptal et.",
        "Monthly": "Ayl\u0131k",
        "Yearly": "Y\u0131ll\u0131k",
        "Free": "\xDCcretsiz",
        "Save 42%": "%42 tasarruf",
        "Turn off Pro (demo)": "Pro'yu kapat (demo)",
        "Turn on Pro (demo)": "Pro'yu a\xE7 (demo)",
        "No pay-to-win. D$ is only earned by doing.": "Parayla kazanmak yok. D$ yaln\u0131zca yaparak kazan\u0131l\u0131r.",
        "No selling your data.": "Verilerin sat\u0131lmaz.",
        "No manipulative streaks or fake urgency.": "Manip\xFClatif seriler ya da sahte aciliyet yok.",
        "Guided meditations, sound waves and a focus timer.": "Sesli meditasyonlar, ses dalgalar\u0131 ve odak zamanlay\u0131c\u0131s\u0131.",
        "Meditate & focus": "Meditasyon ve odak",
        "11 guided meditations \xB7 sound waves \xB7 focus timer": "11 rehberli meditasyon \xB7 ses dalgalar\u0131 \xB7 odak sayac\u0131",
        "Focus & meditations": "Odak ve meditasyonlar",
        "Guided sessions and sound waves": "Rehberli seanslar ve ses dalgalar\u0131",
        "Your future is built before breakfast or not at all.": "Gelece\u011Fin kahvalt\u0131dan \xF6nce kurulur \u2014 ya da hi\xE7.",
        "One kept promise to yourself outweighs a hundred plans.": "Kendine tuttu\u011Fun tek s\xF6z, y\xFCz plandan a\u011F\u0131r basar.",
        "The life you want is on the other side of the task you avoid.": "\u0130stedi\u011Fin hayat, ka\xE7\u0131nd\u0131\u011F\u0131n i\u015Fin \xF6b\xFCr taraf\u0131nda.",
        "Start before you feel ready. Readiness follows action.": "Haz\u0131r hissetmeden ba\u015Fla. Haz\u0131rl\u0131k, eylemin pe\u015Finden gelir.",
        "Discipline is choosing the same future twice.": "Disiplin, ayn\u0131 gelece\u011Fi iki kez se\xE7mektir.",
        "Today's ten minutes beat tomorrow's two hours.": "Bug\xFCn\xFCn on dakikas\u0131, yar\u0131n\u0131n iki saatini yener.",
        "You don't find time. You take it.": "Zaman bulunmaz. Al\u0131n\u0131r.",
        "Small decisions, kept daily, become an unrecognizable life.": "Her g\xFCn tutulan k\xFC\xE7\xFCk kararlar, tan\u0131nmaz bir hayata d\xF6n\xFC\u015F\xFCr.",
        "Motivation is a visitor. Habit is a resident.": "Motivasyon misafirdir. Al\u0131\u015Fkanl\u0131k ev sahibidir.",
        "The dream doesn't need you to be perfect. It needs you to show up.": "Hayalin m\xFCkemmel olman\u0131 beklemiyor. Gelmeni bekliyor.",
        "Every avoided decision is a decision to stay.": "Ka\xE7\u0131n\u0131lan her karar, oldu\u011Fun yerde kalma karar\u0131d\u0131r.",
        "Do the hard thing first. The day gets lighter.": "\xD6nce zor olan\u0131 yap. G\xFCn hafifler.",
        "You are always one decision away from a different day.": "Farkl\u0131 bir g\xFCnden hep tek karar uzaktas\u0131n.",
        "What you repeat, you become.": "Neyi tekrar edersen o olursun.",
        "Done today is stronger than perfect someday.": "Bug\xFCn biten, bir g\xFCn m\xFCkemmel olacaktan g\xFC\xE7l\xFCd\xFCr.",
        "Quiet mornings build loud futures.": "Sessiz sabahlar, g\xFCr gelecekler kurar.",
        "Don't negotiate with the alarm. Negotiate with your future.": "Alarmla pazarl\u0131k etme. Gelece\u011Finle pazarl\u0131k et.",
        "Effort compounds in silence.": "Emek, sessizlikte birikir.",
        "The version of you in three years is watching today.": "\xDC\xE7 y\u0131l sonraki sen, bug\xFCn\xFC izliyor.",
        "A focused hour is a vote for the life you said you wanted.": "Odaklanm\u0131\u015F bir saat, istedi\u011Fini s\xF6yledi\u011Fin hayata verilmi\u015F bir oydur.",
        "Comfort is expensive. It costs the future.": "Konfor pahal\u0131d\u0131r. Bedeli gelecektir.",
        "Begin. The bridge appears as you walk.": "Ba\u015Fla. K\xF6pr\xFC, y\xFCr\xFCd\xFCk\xE7e belirir.",
        "Nobody is coming. That is the good news.": "Kimse gelmiyor. \u0130yi haber de bu.",
        "Protect the first hour and the day protects itself.": "\u0130lk saati koru, g\xFCn kendini korur.",
        "You can't think your way into a new life. You act your way there.": "Yeni bir hayata d\xFC\u015F\xFCnerek varamazs\u0131n. Yaparak var\u0131rs\u0131n.",
        "The task shrinks the moment you touch it.": "\u0130\u015F, dokundu\u011Fun anda k\xFC\xE7\xFCl\xFCr.",
        "Keep the promise small enough to keep.": "S\xF6z\xFC, tutabilece\u011Fin kadar k\xFC\xE7\xFCk ver.",
        "Rest is part of the work. Escape is not.": "Dinlenmek i\u015Fin par\xE7as\u0131d\u0131r. Ka\xE7mak de\u011Fildir.",
        "Direction beats speed. Choose, then walk.": "Y\xF6n, h\u0131z\u0131 yener. Se\xE7 ve y\xFCr\xFC.",
        "Your habits are voting for a future. Check the ballot.": "Al\u0131\u015Fkanl\u0131klar\u0131n bir gelece\u011Fe oy veriyor. Pusulaya bak.",
        "The excuse also takes energy. Spend it on the task.": "Bahane de enerji ister. Onu i\u015Fe harca.",
        "One honest page beats a week of intentions.": "D\xFCr\xFCst bir sayfa, bir haftal\u0131k niyeti yener.",
        "Show up on the gray days. That's where the gap closes.": "Gri g\xFCnlerde de gel. Ara, orada kapan\u0131r.",
        "The future doesn't arrive. It accumulates.": "Gelecek gelmez. Birikir.",
        "Choose the discomfort that pays rent.": "Kar\u015F\u0131l\u0131\u011F\u0131 olan rahats\u0131zl\u0131\u011F\u0131 se\xE7.",
        "Waiting is also a habit. Break it like one.": "Beklemek de bir al\u0131\u015Fkanl\u0131kt\u0131r. Onu da \xF6yle k\u0131r.",
        "Make it easy to start and hard to quit.": "Ba\u015Flamay\u0131 kolayla\u015Ft\u0131r, b\u0131rakmay\u0131 zorla\u015Ft\u0131r.",
        "A calm mind is a working tool, not a luxury.": "Sakin zihin l\xFCks de\u011Fil, \xE7al\u0131\u015Fan bir alettir.",
        "Today is the oldest you've been and the youngest you'll be. Use it.": "Bug\xFCn, oldu\u011Fun en ya\u015Fl\u0131 ve olaca\u011F\u0131n en gen\xE7 g\xFCn\xFCn. Kullan.",
        "Your attention is the currency. Spend it like money.": "Dikkatin bir para birimidir. Onu para gibi harca.",
        "Finish something small before noon.": "\xD6\u011Flenden \xF6nce k\xFC\xE7\xFCk bir \u015Feyi bitir.",
        "The plan is not the work.": "Plan, i\u015Fin kendisi de\u011Fildir.",
        "Doubt gets a vote, not a veto.": "\u015E\xFCphenin oyu olur, vetosu olmaz.",
        "You water what you look at. Look at the dream.": "Neye bakarsan onu sulars\u0131n. Hayaline bak.",
        "Slow is fine. Stopped is the only failure.": "Yava\u015F olmak sorun de\u011Fil. Tek ba\u015Far\u0131s\u0131zl\u0131k durmakt\u0131r.",
        "Say no to the good so you can say yes to the built.": "\u0130yiye hay\u0131r de ki kurdu\u011Funa evet diyebilesin.",
        "Your environment is a decision you make once and obey daily.": "Ortam\u0131n, bir kez verip her g\xFCn itaat etti\u011Fin bir karard\u0131r.",
        "Act like the person you wrote about last night.": "D\xFCn gece hakk\u0131nda yazd\u0131\u011F\u0131n ki\u015Fi gibi davran.",
        "The first rep is the decision. The rest is momentum.": "\u0130lk tekrar karard\u0131r. Gerisi ivmedir.",
        "Don't count the days you missed. Count the one in front of you.": "Ka\xE7\u0131rd\u0131\u011F\u0131n g\xFCnleri sayma. \xD6n\xFCndekini say.",
        "A short walk fixes more than a long scroll.": "K\u0131sa bir y\xFCr\xFCy\xFC\u015F, uzun bir kayd\u0131rmadan \xE7ok \u015Fey d\xFCzeltir.",
        "Earn the evening.": "Ak\u015Fam\u0131 hak et.",
        "Write it down. The mind is for deciding, not storing.": "Yaz. Zihin karar vermek i\xE7indir, depolamak i\xE7in de\u011Fil.",
        "What scares you at 9 is done by 9:20 if you start at 9.": "Dokuzda korkutan i\u015F, dokuzda ba\u015Flarsan dokuz yirmide biter.",
        "Consistency looks boring for weeks and unbelievable in a year.": "\u0130stikrar haftalarca s\u0131k\u0131c\u0131 g\xF6r\xFCn\xFCr, bir y\u0131l sonra inan\u0131lmaz.",
        "You built today's normal. You can build a different one.": "Bug\xFCn\xFCn normalini sen kurdun. Farkl\u0131s\u0131n\u0131 da kurabilirsin.",
        "Ask less of the mood and more of the calendar.": "Ruh halinden az, takvimden \xE7ok \u015Fey iste.",
        "The distance between you and the dream is measured in kept days.": "Seninle hayalin aras\u0131ndaki mesafe, tutulan g\xFCnlerle \xF6l\xE7\xFCl\xFCr.",
        "Decide once, in the morning, and let the day obey.": "Sabah bir kez karar ver, g\xFCn itaat etsin.",
        "Indeed, with hardship comes ease.": "\u015E\xFCphesiz zorlukla beraber bir kolayl\u0131k vard\u0131r.",
        "Quran 94:6": "Kur'an, \u0130n\u015Firah 94:6",
        "God does not change the condition of a people until they change what is in themselves.": "Bir toplum kendinde olan\u0131 de\u011Fi\u015Ftirmedik\xE7e, Allah onlar\u0131n durumunu de\u011Fi\u015Ftirmez.",
        "Quran 13:11": "Kur'an, Ra'd 13:11",
        "Man shall have nothing but what he strives for.": "\u0130nsan i\xE7in ancak \xE7al\u0131\u015Ft\u0131\u011F\u0131n\u0131n kar\u015F\u0131l\u0131\u011F\u0131 vard\u0131r.",
        "Quran 53:39": "Kur'an, Necm 53:39",
        "God does not burden a soul beyond what it can bear.": "Allah hi\xE7 kimseye ta\u015F\u0131yabilece\u011Finden fazlas\u0131n\u0131 y\xFCklemez.",
        "Quran 2:286": "Kur'an, Bakara 2:286",
        "Do not despair of the mercy of God.": "Allah'\u0131n rahmetinden \xFCmidinizi kesmeyin.",
        "Quran 39:53": "Kur'an, Z\xFCmer 39:53",
        "Whoever puts their trust in God \u2014 He is enough for them.": "Kim Allah'a g\xFCvenirse, O ona yeter.",
        "Quran 65:3": "Kur'an, Talak 65:3",
        "Seek help through patience and prayer.": "Sab\u0131r ve namazla yard\u0131m isteyin.",
        "Quran 2:153": "Kur'an, Bakara 2:153",
        "Those who strive for Us \u2014 We will surely guide them to Our ways.": "Bizim u\u011Frumuzda \xE7aba g\xF6sterenleri elbette yollar\u0131m\u0131za eri\u015Ftiririz.",
        "Quran 29:69": "Kur'an, Ankebut 29:69",
        "Do not lose hope, nor be sad.": "Gev\u015Femeyin, \xFCz\xFClmeyin.",
        "Quran 3:139": "Kur'an, \xC2l-i \u0130mran 3:139",
        "Say: My Lord, increase me in knowledge.": "De ki: Rabbim, ilmimi art\u0131r.",
        "Quran 20:114": "Kur'an, T\xE2h\xE2 20:114",
        "When you have decided, put your trust in God.": "Karar verdi\u011Finde art\u0131k Allah'a dayan.",
        "Quran 3:159": "Kur'an, \xC2l-i \u0130mran 3:159",
        "Be patient; indeed, the promise of God is truth.": "Sabret; \u015F\xFCphesiz Allah'\u0131n vaadi hakt\u0131r.",
        "Quran 30:60": "Kur'an, Rum 30:60",
        "If you are grateful, I will surely increase you.": "\u015E\xFCkrederseniz elbette size art\u0131r\u0131r\u0131m.",
        "Quran 14:7": "Kur'an, \u0130brahim 14:7",
        "God is with the patient.": "Allah sabredenlerle beraberdir.",
        "By time, surely mankind is in loss \u2014 except those who believe and do good.": "Zamana yemin olsun ki insan ziyandad\u0131r; iman edip iyi i\u015Fler yapanlar m\xFCstesna.",
        "Quran 103:1-3": "Kur'an, Asr 103:1-3",
        "Remember Me, and I will remember you.": "Beni an\u0131n ki ben de sizi anay\u0131m.",
        "Quran 2:152": "Kur'an, Bakara 2:152",
        "My success is only through God.": "Ba\u015Far\u0131m ancak Allah'tand\u0131r.",
        "Quran 11:88": "Kur'an, Hud 11:88",
        "Hearts find rest in the remembrance of God.": "Kalpler ancak Allah'\u0131 anmakla huzur bulur.",
        "Quran 13:28": "Kur'an, Ra'd 13:28",
        "Whoever does an atom's weight of good will see it.": "Kim zerre kadar iyilik yaparsa onu g\xF6r\xFCr.",
        "Quran 99:7": "Kur'an, Zilzal 99:7",
        "Your Lord has not forsaken you, nor does He hate you. The future will be better for you than the past.": "Rabbin seni b\u0131rakmad\u0131 ve sana dar\u0131lmad\u0131. Sonras\u0131 senin i\xE7in \xF6ncekinden daha hay\u0131rl\u0131 olacak.",
        "Quran 93:3-4": "Kur'an, Duha 93:3-4",
        "Walk the earth and eat of His provision \u2014 to Him is the resurrection.": "Yery\xFCz\xFCnde dola\u015F\u0131n ve O'nun r\u0131zk\u0131ndan yiyin.",
        "Quran 67:15": "Kur'an, M\xFClk 67:15",
        "When the prayer is ended, disperse in the land and seek the bounty of God.": "Namaz bitince yery\xFCz\xFCne da\u011F\u0131l\u0131n ve Allah'\u0131n l\xFCtfundan aray\u0131n.",
        "Quran 62:10": "Kur'an, Cuma 62:10",
        "Speak to people with kindness.": "\u0130nsanlara g\xFCzel s\xF6z s\xF6yleyin.",
        "Quran 2:83": "Kur'an, Bakara 2:83",
        "Repel evil with what is better.": "K\xF6t\xFCl\xFC\u011F\xFC en g\xFCzel olanla sav.",
        "Quran 41:34": "Kur'an, Fussilet 41:34",
        "Do not walk upon the earth with arrogance.": "Yery\xFCz\xFCnde b\xF6b\xFCrlenerek y\xFCr\xFCme.",
        "Quran 17:37": "Kur'an, \u0130sra 17:37",
        "Indeed, God loves those who rely upon Him.": "\u015E\xFCphesiz Allah, kendisine g\xFCvenenleri sever.",
        "Be just; that is nearer to righteousness.": "Adil olun; bu takvaya daha yak\u0131nd\u0131r.",
        "Quran 5:8": "Kur'an, M\xE2ide 5:8",
        "Give the relative his right, and the poor and the traveler.": "Akrabaya, yoksula ve yolda kalm\u0131\u015Fa hakk\u0131n\u0131 ver.",
        "Quran 17:26": "Kur'an, \u0130sra 17:26",
        "And He found you lost and guided you.": "Seni yolunu ararken bulup do\u011Fru yola iletmedi mi?",
        "Quran 93:7": "Kur'an, Duha 93:7",
        "So when you are free, labor on, and to your Lord direct your longing.": "Bir i\u015Fi bitirince hemen ba\u015Fka bir i\u015Fe koyul ve yaln\u0131z Rabbine y\xF6nel.",
        "Quran 94:7-8": "Kur'an, \u0130n\u015Firah 94:7-8",
        "Waste no more time arguing what a good man should be. Be one.": "\u0130yi bir insan\u0131n nas\u0131l olmas\u0131 gerekti\u011Fini tart\u0131\u015Farak vakit kaybetme. \xD6yle biri ol.",
        "Marcus Aurelius": "Marcus Aurelius",
        "You have power over your mind, not outside events. Realize this, and you will find strength.": "D\u0131\u015F olaylara de\u011Fil, zihnine h\xFCkmedebilirsin. Bunu kavra, g\xFCc\xFC bulursun.",
        "It is not that we have a short time to live, but that we waste much of it.": "\xD6mr\xFCm\xFCz k\u0131sa de\u011Fil; biz onun \xE7o\u011Funu israf ediyoruz.",
        "Seneca": "Seneca",
        "Luck is what happens when preparation meets opportunity.": "\u015Eans, haz\u0131rl\u0131\u011F\u0131n f\u0131rsatla bulu\u015Ftu\u011Fu and\u0131r.",
        "Begin at once to live, and count each separate day as a separate life.": "Ya\u015Famaya hemen ba\u015Fla ve her g\xFCn\xFC ayr\u0131 bir \xF6m\xFCr say.",
        "No man is free who is not master of himself.": "Kendine h\xFCkmedemeyen hi\xE7 kimse \xF6zg\xFCr de\u011Fildir.",
        "Epictetus": "Epiktetos",
        "First say to yourself what you would be; and then do what you have to do.": "\xD6nce ne olaca\u011F\u0131n\u0131 kendine s\xF6yle; sonra yapman gerekeni yap.",
        "Yesterday I was clever, so I wanted to change the world. Today I am wise, so I am changing myself.": "D\xFCn zekiydim, d\xFCnyay\u0131 de\u011Fi\u015Ftirmek istedim. Bug\xFCn bilgeyim, kendimi de\u011Fi\u015Ftiriyorum.",
        "Rumi": "Mevl\xE2n\xE2",
        "As you start to walk on the way, the way appears.": "Yola \xE7\u0131kmaya ba\u015Flad\u0131\u011F\u0131nda yol g\xF6r\xFCn\xFCr.",
        "Either exist as you are, or be as you look.": "Ya oldu\u011Fun gibi g\xF6r\xFCn, ya g\xF6r\xFCnd\xFC\u011F\xFCn gibi ol.",
        "Patience is the key to joy.": "Sab\u0131r, sevincin anahtar\u0131d\u0131r.",
        "It does not matter how slowly you go as long as you do not stop.": "Durmad\u0131\u011F\u0131n s\xFCrece ne kadar yava\u015F gitti\u011Finin \xF6nemi yok.",
        "Confucius": "Konf\xFC\xE7y\xFCs",
        "The man who moves a mountain begins by carrying away small stones.": "Da\u011F\u0131 ta\u015F\u0131yan adam, k\xFC\xE7\xFCk ta\u015Flar\u0131 ta\u015F\u0131yarak ba\u015Flar.",
        "When it is obvious that the goals cannot be reached, don't adjust the goals; adjust the action steps.": "Hedefe ula\u015F\u0131lamad\u0131\u011F\u0131 g\xF6r\xFCl\xFCyorsa hedefi de\u011Fil, ad\u0131mlar\u0131 de\u011Fi\u015Ftir.",
        "A journey of a thousand miles begins with a single step.": "Bin millik yolculuk tek bir ad\u0131mla ba\u015Flar.",
        "Lao Tzu": "Lao Tzu",
        "He who conquers others is strong; he who conquers himself is mighty.": "Ba\u015Fkalar\u0131n\u0131 yenen g\xFC\xE7l\xFCd\xFCr; kendini yenen kudretlidir.",
        "We are what we repeatedly do. Excellence, then, is not an act, but a habit.": "Neyi s\xFCrekli yap\u0131yorsak oyuz. M\xFCkemmellik bir eylem de\u011Fil, al\u0131\u015Fkanl\u0131kt\u0131r.",
        "Aristotle": "Aristoteles",
        "Through discipline comes freedom.": "\xD6zg\xFCrl\xFCk disiplinden ge\xE7er.",
        "The beginning is the most important part of the work.": "Ba\u015Flang\u0131\xE7, i\u015Fin en \xF6nemli k\u0131sm\u0131d\u0131r.",
        "Plato": "Platon",
        "An unexamined life is not worth living.": "Sorgulanmam\u0131\u015F bir hayat ya\u015Fanmaya de\u011Fmez.",
        "Socrates": "Sokrates",
        "Knowing yourself is the beginning of all wisdom.": "Kendini bilmek, b\xFCt\xFCn bilgeli\u011Fin ba\u015Flang\u0131c\u0131d\u0131r.",
        "What you seek is seeking you.": "Arad\u0131\u011F\u0131n \u015Fey de seni ar\u0131yor.",
        "Come, come, whoever you are. Ours is not a caravan of despair.": "Gel, gel, ne olursan ol yine gel. Bizim kervan\u0131m\u0131z umutsuzluk kervan\u0131 de\u011Fildir.",
        "Let the beauty of what you love be what you do.": "Sevdi\u011Fin \u015Feyin g\xFCzelli\u011Fi, yapt\u0131\u011F\u0131n i\u015F olsun.",
        "Knowledge is knowing yourself.": "\u0130lim, kendini bilmektir.",
        "Yunus Emre": "Yunus Emre",
        "Let us know one another; the world will remain to no one.": "Gelin tan\u0131\u015F olal\u0131m; d\xFCnya kimseye kalmaz.",
        "He who has no patience has no wisdom.": "Sabr\u0131 olmayan\u0131n hikmeti de olmaz.",
        "Saadi": "Sadi \u015Eirazi",
        "Have patience. All things are difficult before they become easy.": "Sabret. Her \u015Fey kolayla\u015Fmadan \xF6nce zordur.",
        "Doubt is the origin of wisdom.": "\u015E\xFCphe, bilgeli\u011Fin ba\u015Flang\u0131c\u0131d\u0131r.",
        "Descartes": "Descartes",
        "It is not enough to have a good mind; the main thing is to use it well.": "\u0130yi bir akla sahip olmak yetmez; esas olan onu iyi kullanmakt\u0131r.",
        "He who is not courageous enough to take risks will accomplish nothing in life.": "Risk alacak cesareti olmayan, hayatta hi\xE7bir \u015Fey ba\u015Faramaz.",
        "Ibn Khaldun": "\u0130bn Haldun",
        "The past resembles the future more than one drop of water resembles another.": "Ge\xE7mi\u015F, gelece\u011Fe bir damla suyun di\u011Ferine benzedi\u011Finden daha \xE7ok benzer.",
        "Knowledge without action is madness, and action without knowledge is vanity.": "Amelsiz ilim delilik, ilimsiz amel bo\u015Funad\u0131r.",
        "Al-Ghazali": "Gaz\xE2l\xEE",
        "Well begun is half done.": "\u0130yi ba\u015Flamak, yar\u0131 yar\u0131ya bitirmektir.",
        "Do not wait to strike till the iron is hot; make it hot by striking.": "Demir tav\u0131na gelsin diye bekleme; d\xF6verek tav\u0131na getir.",
        "W. B. Yeats": "W. B. Yeats",
        "Lost time is never found again.": "Kaybedilen zaman bir daha bulunmaz.",
        "Benjamin Franklin": "Benjamin Franklin",
        "Energy and persistence conquer all things.": "Enerji ve sebat her \u015Feyin \xFCstesinden gelir.",
        "Knowing is not enough; we must apply. Willing is not enough; we must do.": "Bilmek yetmez, uygulamal\u0131y\u0131z. \u0130stemek yetmez, yapmal\u0131y\u0131z.",
        "Goethe": "Goethe",
        "Whatever you can do, or dream you can, begin it. Boldness has genius, power, and magic in it.": "Yapabilece\u011Fin ya da hayal etti\u011Fin ne varsa ba\u015Fla. Cesarette deha, g\xFC\xE7 ve sihir vard\u0131r.",
        "Nietzsche": "Nietzsche",
        "That which does not kill us makes us stronger.": "Bizi \xF6ld\xFCrmeyen \u015Fey g\xFC\xE7lendirir.",
        "Everyone thinks of changing the world, but no one thinks of changing himself.": "Herkes d\xFCnyay\u0131 de\u011Fi\u015Ftirmeyi d\xFC\u015F\xFCn\xFCr, kimse kendini de\u011Fi\u015Ftirmeyi d\xFC\u015F\xFCnmez.",
        "Tolstoy": "Tolstoy",
        "The two most powerful warriors are patience and time.": "En g\xFC\xE7l\xFC iki sava\u015F\xE7\u0131 sab\u0131r ve zamand\u0131r.",
        "It had long since come to my attention that people of accomplishment rarely sat back and let things happen to them. They went out and happened to things.": "Ba\u015Faran insanlar\u0131n olaylar\u0131 beklemedi\u011Fini, gidip olaylar\u0131n ba\u015F\u0131na ge\xE7ti\u011Fini \xE7oktand\u0131r fark etmi\u015Ftim.",
        "Leonardo da Vinci": "Leonardo da Vinci",
        "Simplicity is the ultimate sophistication.": "Sadelik, inceli\u011Fin zirvesidir.",
        "Plutarch": "Plutarkhos",
        "Success is not final, failure is not fatal: it is the courage to continue that counts.": "Ba\u015Far\u0131 son de\u011Fildir, ba\u015Far\u0131s\u0131zl\u0131k \xF6l\xFCmc\xFCl de\u011Fildir; as\u0131l olan devam etme cesaretidir.",
        "Winston Churchill": "Winston Churchill",
        "The best way to predict the future is to create it.": "Gelece\u011Fi \xF6ng\xF6rmenin en iyi yolu onu in\u015Fa etmektir.",
        "Abraham Lincoln": "Abraham Lincoln",
        "What lies behind us and what lies before us are tiny matters compared to what lies within us.": "Ard\u0131m\u0131zda ve \xF6n\xFCm\xFCzde duranlar, i\xE7imizde duran\u0131n yan\u0131nda k\xFC\xE7\xFCk kal\u0131r.",
        "Emerson": "Emerson",
        "Do not go where the path may lead; go instead where there is no path and leave a trail.": "Yolun g\xF6t\xFCrd\xFC\u011F\xFC yere de\u011Fil, yol olmayan yere git ve iz b\u0131rak.",
        "Go confidently in the direction of your dreams. Live the life you have imagined.": "Hayallerinin y\xF6n\xFCnde g\xFCvenle ilerle. Hayal etti\u011Fin hayat\u0131 ya\u015Fa.",
        "Thoreau": "Thoreau",
        "If one advances confidently toward his dreams, he will meet with a success unexpected in common hours.": "Hayallerine g\xFCvenle y\xFCr\xFCyen, s\u0131radan saatlerde beklenmedik bir ba\u015Far\u0131yla kar\u015F\u0131la\u015F\u0131r.",
        "There is nothing impossible to him who will try.": "Deneyen i\xE7in imk\xE2ns\u0131z yoktur.",
        "Alexander the Great": "B\xFCy\xFCk \u0130skender",
        "A goal without a plan is just a wish.": "Plan\u0131 olmayan hedef, yaln\u0131zca bir dilektir.",
        "Antoine de Saint-Exup\xE9ry": "Antoine de Saint-Exup\xE9ry",
        "The day you plant the seed is not the day you eat the fruit. Plant anyway.": "Tohumu ekti\u011Fin g\xFCn meyveyi yedi\u011Fin g\xFCn de\u011Fildir. Yine de ek.",
        "Courage is a decision repeated quietly every morning.": "Cesaret, her sabah sessizce tekrarlanan bir karard\u0131r.",
        "Your dream has a price in days. Start paying.": "Hayalinin g\xFCn cinsinden bir bedeli var. \xD6demeye ba\u015Fla.",
        "Read a page, walk a mile, keep a word. That is a good day.": "Bir sayfa oku, bir yol y\xFCr\xFC, bir s\xF6z tut. \u0130yi bir g\xFCn budur.",
        "The mountain is climbed by the one who is still walking at noon.": "Da\u011Fa, \xF6\u011Flen h\xE2l\xE2 y\xFCr\xFCmekte olan \xE7\u0131kar.",
        "If I have seen further, it is by standing on the shoulders of giants.": "Daha uza\u011F\u0131 g\xF6rebildiysem, devlerin omuzlar\u0131nda durdu\u011Fum i\xE7indir.",
        "Isaac Newton": "Isaac Newton",
        "Genius is one percent inspiration and ninety-nine percent perspiration.": "Deha, y\xFCzde bir ilham ve y\xFCzde doksan dokuz terdir.",
        "Thomas Edison": "Thomas Edison",
        "I have not failed. I've just found ten thousand ways that won't work.": "Ba\u015Far\u0131s\u0131z olmad\u0131m. Sadece i\u015Fe yaramayan on bin yol buldum.",
        "Nothing in life is to be feared, it is only to be understood.": "Hayatta hi\xE7bir \u015Feyden korkulmaz; her \u015Fey yaln\u0131zca anla\u015F\u0131lmay\u0131 bekler.",
        "Marie Curie": "Marie Curie",
        "Be less curious about people and more curious about ideas.": "\u0130nsanlar\u0131 de\u011Fil, fikirleri daha \xE7ok merak et.",
        "Life is like riding a bicycle. To keep your balance, you must keep moving.": "Hayat bisiklete binmek gibidir. Dengeni korumak i\xE7in hareket etmeye devam etmelisin.",
        "Albert Einstein": "Albert Einstein",
        "In the middle of difficulty lies opportunity.": "Zorlu\u011Fun ortas\u0131nda f\u0131rsat yatar.",
        "Imagination is more important than knowledge.": "Hayal g\xFCc\xFC bilgiden daha \xF6nemlidir.",
        "The present is theirs; the future, for which I really worked, is mine.": "Bug\xFCn onlar\u0131n; as\u0131l u\u011Fruna \xE7al\u0131\u015Ft\u0131\u011F\u0131m gelecek benimdir.",
        "Nikola Tesla": "Nikola Tesla",
        "Chance favors the prepared mind.": "\u015Eans, haz\u0131rl\u0131kl\u0131 zihinden yanad\u0131r.",
        "Louis Pasteur": "Louis Pasteur",
        "Nothing is too wonderful to be true, if it be consistent with the laws of nature.": "Do\u011Fa yasalar\u0131yla uyumluysa, hi\xE7bir \u015Fey ger\xE7ek olamayacak kadar harika de\u011Fildir.",
        "Michael Faraday": "Michael Faraday",
        "It is not the strongest of the species that survives, but the one most responsive to change.": "Hayatta kalan t\xFCrlerin en g\xFC\xE7l\xFCs\xFC de\u011Fil, de\u011Fi\u015Fime en iyi uyum sa\u011Flayan\u0131d\u0131r.",
        "Charles Darwin": "Charles Darwin",
        "Measure what is measurable, and make measurable what is not so.": "\xD6l\xE7\xFClebileni \xF6l\xE7; \xF6l\xE7\xFClemeyeni \xF6l\xE7\xFClebilir k\u0131l.",
        "Galileo Galilei": "Galileo Galilei",
        "Give me a place to stand, and I will move the earth.": "Bana bir dayanak noktas\u0131 verin, d\xFCnyay\u0131 yerinden oynatay\u0131m.",
        "Archimedes": "Ar\u015Fimet",
        "Knowledge is the treasure, and practice is the key to it.": "Bilgi hazinedir, uygulamak onun anahtar\u0131d\u0131r.",
        "Ibn Sina": "\u0130bn Sina",
        "The width of life is more important than its length.": "Hayat\u0131n geni\u015Fli\u011Fi, uzunlu\u011Fundan daha \xF6nemlidir.",
        "Science is the great antidote to the poison of ignorance.": "Bilim, cehalet zehrinin en b\xFCy\xFCk panzehiridir.",
        "Adam Smith": "Adam Smith",
        "Be the change that you wish to see in the world.": "D\xFCnyada g\xF6rmek istedi\u011Fin de\u011Fi\u015Fimin kendisi ol.",
        "Mahatma Gandhi": "Mahatma Gandhi",
        "Strength does not come from physical capacity. It comes from an indomitable will.": "G\xFC\xE7 bedenden de\u011Fil, boyun e\u011Fmeyen iradeden gelir.",
        "Live as if you were to die tomorrow. Learn as if you were to live forever.": "Yar\u0131n \xF6lecekmi\u015F gibi ya\u015Fa, hi\xE7 \xF6lmeyecekmi\u015F gibi \xF6\u011Fren.",
        "It always seems impossible until it is done.": "Yap\u0131lana kadar her \u015Fey imk\xE2ns\u0131z g\xF6r\xFCn\xFCr.",
        "Nelson Mandela": "Nelson Mandela",
        "I never lose. I either win or learn.": "Asla kaybetmem. Ya kazan\u0131r\u0131m ya \xF6\u011Frenirim.",
        "Do not judge me by my successes; judge me by how many times I fell down and got back up again.": "Beni ba\u015Far\u0131lar\u0131mla de\u011Fil, ka\xE7 kez d\xFC\u015F\xFCp yeniden kalkt\u0131\u011F\u0131mla yarg\u0131la.",
        "You cannot cross the sea merely by standing and staring at the water.": "Denize bak\u0131p durmakla kar\u015F\u0131ya ge\xE7emezsin.",
        "Rabindranath Tagore": "Rabindranath Tagore",
        "Faith is the bird that feels the light when the dawn is still dark.": "\u0130nan\xE7, \u015Fafak hen\xFCz karanl\u0131kken \u0131\u015F\u0131\u011F\u0131 hisseden ku\u015Ftur.",
        "If you can't fly then run, if you can't run then walk, if you can't walk then crawl, but by all means keep moving.": "U\xE7am\u0131yorsan ko\u015F, ko\u015Fam\u0131yorsan y\xFCr\xFC, y\xFCr\xFCyemiyorsan emekle; ama ne olursa olsun ilerlemeye devam et.",
        "Martin Luther King Jr.": "Martin Luther King Jr.",
        "Faith is taking the first step even when you don't see the whole staircase.": "\u0130nan\xE7, merdivenin tamam\u0131n\u0131 g\xF6rmeden ilk basama\u011F\u0131 \xE7\u0131kmakt\u0131r.",
        "The darkest hour has only sixty minutes.": "En karanl\u0131k saatin de yaln\u0131zca altm\u0131\u015F dakikas\u0131 vard\u0131r.",
        "Morris Mandel": "Morris Mandel",
        "Turn your face to the sun and the shadows fall behind you.": "Y\xFCz\xFCn\xFC g\xFCne\u015Fe d\xF6n, g\xF6lgeler arkanda kals\u0131n.",
        "Maori proverb": "Maori atas\xF6z\xFC",
        "Fall seven times, stand up eight.": "Yedi kez d\xFC\u015F, sekiz kez kalk.",
        "Japanese proverb": "Japon atas\xF6z\xFC",
        "The best time to plant a tree was twenty years ago. The second best time is now.": "A\u011Fa\xE7 dikmenin en iyi zaman\u0131 yirmi y\u0131l \xF6nceydi. \u0130kinci en iyi zaman \u015Fimdi.",
        "Chinese proverb": "\xC7in atas\xF6z\xFC",
        "If you want to go fast, go alone. If you want to go far, go together.": "H\u0131zl\u0131 gitmek istersen yaln\u0131z git, uza\u011Fa gitmek istersen birlikte git.",
        "African proverb": "Afrika atas\xF6z\xFC",
        "However long the night, the dawn will break.": "Gece ne kadar uzun olursa olsun, \u015Fafak s\xF6ker.",
        "A smooth sea never made a skilled sailor.": "Durgun deniz usta denizci yeti\u015Ftirmez.",
        "English proverb": "\u0130ngiliz atas\xF6z\xFC",
        "Little by little, the bird builds its nest.": "Azar azar, ku\u015F yuvas\u0131n\u0131 yapar.",
        "French proverb": "Frans\u0131z atas\xF6z\xFC",
        "He who rises early, God helps.": "Erken kalkana Tanr\u0131 yard\u0131m eder.",
        "Spanish proverb": "\u0130spanyol atas\xF6z\xFC",
        "Damlaya damlaya g\xF6l olur \u2014 drop by drop, a lake is formed.": "Damlaya damlaya g\xF6l olur.",
        "Turkish proverb": "T\xFCrk atas\xF6z\xFC",
        "The one who walks the road learns more than the one who reads about it.": "Yolu y\xFCr\xFCyen, yolu okuyandan \xE7ok \xF6\u011Frenir.",
        "Anatolian saying": "Anadolu s\xF6z\xFC",
        "Science is the most genuine guide in life.": "Hayatta en hakiki m\xFCr\u015Fit ilimdir.",
        "Mustafa Kemal Atat\xFCrk": "Mustafa Kemal Atat\xFCrk",
        "Hope is the pillar that holds up the world.": "Umut, d\xFCnyay\u0131 ayakta tutan direktir.",
        "Pliny the Elder": "Ya\u015Fl\u0131 Plinius",
        "They can because they think they can.": "Yapabilirler, \xE7\xFCnk\xFC yapabileceklerini d\xFC\u015F\xFCn\xFCyorlar.",
        "Virgil": "Vergilius",
        "Fortune favors the bold.": "Talih, cesurdan yanad\u0131r.",
        "Carpe diem \u2014 seize the day.": "Carpe diem \u2014 g\xFCn\xFC yakala.",
        "Horace": "Horatius",
        "He who is brave is free.": "Cesur olan \xF6zg\xFCrd\xFCr.",
        "Man is affected not by events but by the view he takes of them.": "\u0130nsan\u0131 olaylar de\u011Fil, olaylara bak\u0131\u015F\u0131 etkiler.",
        "Do every act of your life as though it were the very last act of your life.": "Her i\u015Fini, hayat\u0131n\u0131n son i\u015Fiymi\u015F gibi yap.",
        "Very little is needed to make a happy life; it is all within yourself.": "Mutlu bir hayat i\xE7in \xE7ok az \u015Fey gerekir; hepsi senin i\xE7indedir.",
        "Pray as if everything depends on God; work as if everything depends on you.": "Her \u015Fey Allah'a ba\u011Fl\u0131ym\u0131\u015F gibi dua et; her \u015Fey sana ba\u011Fl\u0131ym\u0131\u015F gibi \xE7al\u0131\u015F.",
        "Augustine of Hippo": "Aziz Augustinus",
        "Trust in God, but tie your camel.": "Allah'a tevekk\xFCl et, ama deveni ba\u011Fla.",
        "Prophetic wisdom": "Hadis kaynakl\u0131 hikmet",
        "Actions are judged by intentions.": "Ameller niyetlere g\xF6redir.",
        "The strong is not the one who overcomes people; the strong is the one who controls himself in anger.": "G\xFC\xE7l\xFC, insanlar\u0131 yenen de\u011Fil; \xF6fkelendi\u011Finde kendine h\xE2kim oland\u0131r.",
        "The most beloved deeds to God are those done regularly, even if small.": "Allah kat\u0131nda amellerin en sevimlisi, az da olsa devaml\u0131 olan\u0131d\u0131r.",
        "This world is the field of the hereafter: what you sow here, you harvest there.": "D\xFCnya ahiretin tarlas\u0131d\u0131r: burada ne ekersen orada onu bi\xE7ersin.",
        "Islamic wisdom": "\u0130slami hikmet",
        "Whoever saves himself from his own greed \u2014 those are the successful.": "Kim nefsinin cimrili\u011Finden korunursa, i\u015Fte onlar kurtulu\u015Fa erenlerdir.",
        "Quran 59:9": "Kur'an, Ha\u015Fr 59:9",
        "God is the light of the heavens and the earth.": "Allah, g\xF6klerin ve yerin nurudur.",
        "Quran 24:35": "Kur'an, Nur 24:35",
        "Call upon Me; I will respond to you.": "Bana dua edin, size kar\u015F\u0131l\u0131k vereyim.",
        "Quran 40:60": "Kur'an, M\xFC'min 40:60",
        "It may be that you dislike a thing and it is good for you.": "Ho\u015Flanmad\u0131\u011F\u0131n\u0131z bir \u015Fey sizin i\xE7in hay\u0131rl\u0131 olabilir.",
        "Quran 2:216": "Kur'an, Bakara 2:216",
        "And your Lord is going to give you, and you will be satisfied.": "Rabbin sana verecek ve sen raz\u0131 olacaks\u0131n.",
        "Quran 93:5": "Kur'an, Duha 93:5",
        "Peace begins with a smile.": "Huzur bir g\xFCl\xFCmsemeyle ba\u015Flar.",
        "Mother Teresa": "Rahibe Teresa",
        "Not all of us can do great things. But we can do small things with great love.": "Hepimiz b\xFCy\xFCk i\u015Fler yapamay\u0131z. Ama k\xFC\xE7\xFCk i\u015Fleri b\xFCy\xFCk sevgiyle yapabiliriz.",
        "Where there is no vision, the people perish.": "Vizyonun olmad\u0131\u011F\u0131 yerde halk yok olur.",
        "Proverbs 29:18": "S\xFCleyman'\u0131n \xD6zdeyi\u015Fleri 29:18",
        "Whatever your hand finds to do, do it with all your might.": "Elin ne i\u015F bulursa, onu b\xFCt\xFCn g\xFCc\xFCnle yap.",
        "Ecclesiastes 9:10": "Vaiz 9:10",
        "The energy of the mind is the essence of life.": "Zihnin enerjisi, hayat\u0131n \xF6z\xFCd\xFCr.",
        "Where attention goes, energy flows.": "Dikkat nereye giderse enerji oraya akar.",
        "Huna wisdom": "Huna \xF6\u011Fretisi",
        "What you think, you become. What you feel, you attract.": "Ne d\xFC\u015F\xFCn\xFCrsen o olursun; ne hissedersen onu \xE7ekersin.",
        "Buddhist wisdom": "Budist \xF6\u011Freti",
        "The mind is everything.": "Zihin her \u015Feydir.",
        "Each morning we are born again. What we do today is what matters most.": "Her sabah yeniden do\u011Far\u0131z. As\u0131l \xF6nemli olan bug\xFCn yapt\u0131klar\u0131m\u0131zd\u0131r.",
        "Drop by drop is the water pot filled.": "Su kab\u0131 damla damla dolar.",
        "A man is but the product of his thoughts; what he thinks, he becomes.": "\u0130nsan d\xFC\u015F\xFCncelerinin \xFCr\xFCn\xFCd\xFCr; ne d\xFC\u015F\xFCn\xFCrse o olur.",
        "Be patient, outdo one another in patience, and remain steadfast, so that you may succeed.": "Sabret, sab\u0131rda yar\u0131\u015F ve kararl\u0131 dur ki kurtulu\u015Fa eresin.",
        "Quran 3:200": "Kur'an, \xC2l-i \u0130mran 3:200",
        "God is enough for us, and He is the best guardian of our affairs.": "Allah bize yeter; O ne g\xFCzel vekildir.",
        "Quran 3:173": "Kur'an, \xC2l-i \u0130mran 3:173",
        "Do not grieve; indeed, God is with us.": "\xDCz\xFClme; \u015F\xFCphesiz Allah bizimledir.",
        "Quran 9:40": "Kur'an, Tevbe 9:40",
        "I am near \u2014 I answer the call of the one who calls on Me.": "Ben yak\u0131n\u0131m; Bana seslenenin \xE7a\u011Fr\u0131s\u0131na kar\u015F\u0131l\u0131k veririm.",
        "Quran 2:186": "Kur'an, Bakara 2:186",
        "Whoever does good, man or woman, while believing \u2014 We will surely give them a good life.": "Erkek olsun kad\u0131n olsun, kim inanarak iyi i\u015F yaparsa, ona g\xFCzel bir hayat ya\u015Fat\u0131r\u0131z.",
        "Quran 16:97": "Kur'an, Nahl 16:97",
        "Keep up the prayer, encourage what is right, and be patient with whatever befalls you.": "Namaz\u0131 s\xFCrd\xFCr, iyili\u011Fi \xF6\u011F\xFCtle ve ba\u015F\u0131na gelene sabret.",
        "Quran 31:17": "Kur'an, Lokman 31:17",
        "Whoever is patient and forgives \u2014 that is true strength of resolve.": "Kim sabreder ve ba\u011F\u0131\u015Flarsa, i\u015Fte bu, kararl\u0131l\u0131\u011F\u0131n en g\xFC\xE7l\xFCs\xFCd\xFCr.",
        "Quran 42:43": "Kur'an, \u015E\xFBra 42:43",
        "He is with you wherever you are.": "Nerede olursan ol, O seninledir.",
        "Quran 57:4": "Kur'an, Hadid 57:4",
        "Do not grieve over what has passed you by, nor gloat over what you have been given.": "Elinden ka\xE7ana \xFCz\xFClme, sana verilenle de \u015F\u0131marma.",
        "Quran 57:23": "Kur'an, Hadid 57:23",
        "Whoever believes in God \u2014 He guides their heart.": "Kim Allah'a inan\u0131rsa, O onun kalbine yol g\xF6sterir.",
        "Quran 64:11": "Kur'an, Te\u011Fab\xFCn 64:11",
        "Be patient, for God does not let the reward of those who do good be lost.": "Sabret; Allah iyilik yapanlar\u0131n eme\u011Fini bo\u015Fa \xE7\u0131karmaz.",
        "Quran 11:115": "Kur'an, Hud 11:115",
        "The servants of the Merciful walk the earth humbly, and when the ignorant address them, they answer: Peace.": "Rahman'\u0131n kullar\u0131 yery\xFCz\xFCnde al\xE7akg\xF6n\xFCll\xFC y\xFCr\xFCr; cahiller onlara sata\u015Ft\u0131\u011F\u0131nda 'Selam' derler.",
        "Quran 25:63": "Kur'an, Furkan 25:63",
        "Seek the life to come in what God has given you, but do not forget your share of this world.": "Allah'\u0131n sana verdikleriyle ahireti ara; ama bu d\xFCnyadaki pay\u0131n\u0131 da unutma.",
        "Quran 28:77": "Kur'an, Kasas 28:77",
        "Is the reward for good anything but good?": "\u0130yili\u011Fin kar\u015F\u0131l\u0131\u011F\u0131 iyilikten ba\u015Fka ne olabilir?",
        "Quran 55:60": "Kur'an, Rahman 55:60",
        "If you do good, you do it for yourself.": "\u0130yilik edersen, kendine iyilik etmi\u015F olursun.",
        "Quran 17:7": "Kur'an, \u0130sra 17:7",
        "Do good; truly God loves those who do good.": "\u0130yilik yap; \u015F\xFCphesiz Allah iyilik yapanlar\u0131 sever.",
        "Quran 2:195": "Kur'an, Bakara 2:195",
        "Those who are patient will be given their reward without measure.": "Sabredenlere \xF6d\xFClleri hesaps\u0131z verilir.",
        "Quran 39:10": "Kur'an, Z\xFCmer 39:10",
        "Those who restrain their anger and pardon people \u2014 God loves those who do good.": "\xD6fkesini yutanlar ve insanlar\u0131 ba\u011F\u0131\u015Flayanlar \u2014 Allah iyilik edenleri sever.",
        "Quran 3:134": "Kur'an, \xC2l-i \u0130mran 3:134",
        "Truly successful is the one who purifies the soul.": "Nefsini ar\u0131nd\u0131ran ger\xE7ekten kurtulu\u015Fa ermi\u015Ftir.",
        "Quran 91:9": "Kur'an, \u015Eems 91:9",
        "If you tried to count the blessings of God, you could never number them.": "Allah'\u0131n nimetlerini saymaya kalksan, sayamazs\u0131n.",
        "Quran 16:18": "Kur'an, Nahl 16:18",
        "Make things easy, do not make them hard; give good news, do not drive people away.": "Kolayla\u015Ft\u0131r, zorla\u015Ft\u0131rma; m\xFCjdele, nefret ettirme.",
        "The best of people are those most helpful to people.": "\u0130nsanlar\u0131n en hay\u0131rl\u0131s\u0131, insanlara en faydal\u0131 oland\u0131r.",
        "Value your health before illness and your free time before it is filled.": "Hastal\u0131k gelmeden sa\u011Fl\u0131\u011F\u0131n\u0131n, me\u015Fguliyet gelmeden bo\u015F vaktinin k\u0131ymetini bil.",
        "God loves that when you do a piece of work, you do it well.": "Allah, bir i\u015F yapt\u0131\u011F\u0131nda onu g\xFCzel yapman\u0131 sever.",
        "Richness is not having many possessions; richness is contentment of the soul.": "Zenginlik mal \xE7oklu\u011Fu de\u011Fildir; as\u0131l zenginlik g\xF6n\xFCl toklu\u011Fudur.",
        "Be in this world as if you were a traveler passing along a road.": "Bu d\xFCnyada, yoldan ge\xE7en bir yolcu gibi ol.",
        "A kind word is charity.": "G\xFCzel bir s\xF6z sadakad\u0131r.",
        "Whoever walks a path in search of knowledge, God eases their way.": "Kim ilim i\xE7in bir yola girerse, Allah ona yolunu kolayla\u015Ft\u0131r\u0131r.",
        "If the end of the world comes while you hold a sapling in your hand, plant it.": "K\u0131yamet koparken elinde bir fidan varsa, onu dik.",
        "Do not let hardship fill you with despair; stars shine brightest in the darkest night.": "Zorluklar seni umutsuzlu\u011Fa d\xFC\u015F\xFCrmesin; y\u0131ld\u0131zlar en karanl\u0131k gecede parlar.",
        "Ali ibn Abi Talib": "Ali bin Ebu Talib",
        "Patience is of two kinds: patience over what pains you, and patience against what you crave.": "Sab\u0131r iki t\xFCrl\xFCd\xFCr: ac\u0131 verene sab\u0131r ve arzulad\u0131\u011F\u0131na kar\u015F\u0131 sab\u0131r.",
        "Do not be a slave to another when God has created you free.": "Allah seni h\xFCr yaratm\u0131\u015Fken ba\u015Fkas\u0131na kul olma.",
        "Your cure is within you, though you do not see it.": "Derdinin derman\u0131 senin i\xE7indedir, ama sen g\xF6rmezsin.",
        "Hold yourself to account before you are held to account.": "Hesaba \xE7ekilmeden \xF6nce kendini hesaba \xE7ek.",
        "Omar ibn al-Khattab": "Hz. \xD6mer",
        "The most beloved to me is the one who shows me my faults.": "Bana kusurlar\u0131m\u0131 g\xF6steren, en sevdi\u011Fim ki\u015Fidir.",
        "The words you speak become the house you live in.": "S\xF6yledi\u011Fin s\xF6zler, i\xE7inde ya\u015Fad\u0131\u011F\u0131n ev olur.",
        "Hafiz": "H\xE2f\u0131z",
        "Be happy for this moment. This moment is your life.": "Bu an i\xE7in mutlu ol; bu an senin hayat\u0131nd\u0131r.",
        "Omar Khayyam": "\xD6mer Hayyam",
        "The ocean can be yours; why should you settle for a drop of dew?": "Okyanus senin olabilecekken neden bir \xE7iy damlas\u0131yla yetinesin?",
        "Attar": "Ferid\xFCddin Attar",
        "Strive to discover the mystery before life is taken from you.": "Hayat elinden gitmeden s\u0131rr\u0131 ke\u015Ffetmeye \xE7al\u0131\u015F.",
        "He who knows himself knows his Lord.": "Kendini bilen, Rabbini bilir.",
        "Ibn Arabi": "\u0130bn Arabi",
        "A candle loses nothing by lighting another candle.": "Bir mum, ba\u015Fka bir mumu tutu\u015Fturmakla \u0131\u015F\u0131\u011F\u0131ndan bir \u015Fey kaybetmez.",
        "Shams Tabrizi": "\u015Eems-i Tebrizi",
        "Wherever you are, that is the entry point.": "Nerede olursan ol, giri\u015F kap\u0131s\u0131 oras\u0131d\u0131r.",
        "Kabir": "Kabir",
        "The river that flows in you also flows in me.": "Sende akan \u0131rmak bende de akar.",
        "Do not go looking for the garden of flowers; the garden is within you.": "\xC7i\xE7ek bah\xE7esini d\u0131\u015Far\u0131da arama; bah\xE7e senin i\xE7inde.",
        "Raise your words, not your voice. It is rain that grows flowers, not thunder.": "Sesini de\u011Fil, s\xF6z\xFCn\xFC y\xFCkselt. \xC7i\xE7ekleri b\xFCy\xFCten ya\u011Fmurdur, g\xF6k g\xFCr\xFClt\xFCs\xFC de\u011Fil.",
        "You are not a drop in the ocean; you are the entire ocean in a drop.": "Sen okyanusta bir damla de\u011Filsin; bir damlada koca bir okyanussun.",
        "Yesterday is gone and took its story with it; today, sow new seeds.": "D\xFCn gitti, hik\xE2yesini de g\xF6t\xFCrd\xFC; bug\xFCn yeni tohumlar ek.",
        "A traveler without knowledge is a bird without wings.": "\u0130limsiz yolcu, kanats\u0131z ku\u015Fa benzer.",
        "Whatever is made in haste is easily undone.": "Aceleyle yap\u0131lan i\u015F kolayca bozulur.",
        "A little and a little, gathered together, become a great deal.": "Azar azar biriken, sonunda \xE7ok olur.",
        "While we are postponing, life speeds by.": "Biz ertelerken, hayat h\u0131zla ge\xE7ip gider.",
        "If you do not know to which port you are sailing, no wind is favorable.": "Hangi limana gitti\u011Fini bilmiyorsan, hi\xE7bir r\xFCzg\xE2r i\u015Fine yaramaz.",
        "Difficulties strengthen the mind, as labor does the body.": "Zorluklar zihni g\xFC\xE7lendirir, t\u0131pk\u0131 eme\u011Fin bedeni g\xFC\xE7lendirdi\u011Fi gibi.",
        "As long as you live, keep learning how to live.": "Ya\u015Fad\u0131\u011F\u0131n s\xFCrece, ya\u015Famay\u0131 \xF6\u011Frenmeye devam et.",
        "No great thing is created suddenly, any more than a bunch of grapes or a fig.": "Hi\xE7bir b\xFCy\xFCk \u015Fey aniden var olmaz; t\u0131pk\u0131 bir salk\u0131m \xFCz\xFCm ya da bir incir gibi.",
        "Do not explain your philosophy. Embody it.": "Felsefeni anlatma; onu ya\u015Fa.",
        "Circumstances do not make the man; they reveal him to himself.": "Ko\u015Fullar insan\u0131 yapmaz; onu kendisine g\xF6sterir.",
        "The happiness of your life depends upon the quality of your thoughts.": "Hayat\u0131n\u0131n mutlulu\u011Fu, d\xFC\u015F\xFCncelerinin niteli\u011Fine ba\u011Fl\u0131d\u0131r.",
        "Confine yourself to the present.": "Dikkatini \u015Fimdiki anda topla.",
        "If it is not right, do not do it; if it is not true, do not say it.": "Do\u011Fru de\u011Filse yapma; ger\xE7ek de\u011Filse s\xF6yleme.",
        "When you arise in the morning, think of what a precious privilege it is to be alive.": "Sabah uyand\u0131\u011F\u0131nda, ya\u015F\u0131yor olman\u0131n ne b\xFCy\xFCk bir ayr\u0131cal\u0131k oldu\u011Funu d\xFC\u015F\xFCn.",
        "Dwell on the beauty of life. Watch the stars, and see yourself running with them.": "Hayat\u0131n g\xFCzelli\u011Fi \xFCzerine d\xFC\u015F\xFCn. Y\u0131ld\u0131zlar\u0131 izle ve kendini onlarla akarken g\xF6r.",
        "Gratitude is not only the greatest of virtues but the parent of all the others.": "\u015E\xFCkran yaln\u0131zca erdemlerin en b\xFCy\xFC\u011F\xFC de\u011Fil, hepsinin anas\u0131d\u0131r.",
        "Cicero": "\xC7i\xE7ero",
        "While there is life, there is hope.": "Hayat oldu\u011Fu s\xFCrece umut vard\u0131r.",
        "An angry man opens his mouth and shuts his eyes.": "\xD6fkeli insan a\u011Fz\u0131n\u0131 a\xE7ar, g\xF6zlerini kapat\u0131r.",
        "Cato": "Cato",
        "He has the most who is most content with the least.": "En aza en \xE7ok kanaat eden, en \xE7o\u011Fa sahiptir.",
        "Diogenes": "Diyojen",
        "No man ever steps in the same river twice, for it is not the same river and he is not the same man.": "Kimse ayn\u0131 nehre iki kez giremez; \xE7\xFCnk\xFC ne nehir ayn\u0131 nehirdir ne de insan ayn\u0131 insan.",
        "Heraclitus": "Herakleitos",
        "Character is destiny.": "Karakter, kaderdir.",
        "Big results require big ambitions.": "B\xFCy\xFCk sonu\xE7lar, b\xFCy\xFCk hedefler ister.",
        "Do not say a little in many words, but a great deal in few.": "\xC7ok s\xF6zle az \u015Fey s\xF6yleme; az s\xF6zle \xE7ok \u015Fey s\xF6yle.",
        "Pythagoras": "Pisagor",
        "Above all things, respect yourself.": "Her \u015Feyden \xF6nce kendine sayg\u0131 duy.",
        "Well-being is realized by small steps, but it is truly no small thing.": "\u0130yi ya\u015Fam k\xFC\xE7\xFCk ad\u0131mlarla kurulur; ama kendisi asla k\xFC\xE7\xFCk bir \u015Fey de\u011Fildir.",
        "Zeno": "Zenon",
        "We have two ears and one mouth, so we should listen more than we speak.": "\u0130ki kula\u011F\u0131m\u0131z ve bir a\u011Fz\u0131m\u0131z var; demek ki konu\u015Ftu\u011Fumuzdan \xE7ok dinlemeliyiz.",
        "Our doubts are traitors, and make us lose the good we oft might win by fearing to attempt.": "Ku\u015Fkular\u0131m\u0131z birer haindir; denemekten korkutarak kazanabilece\u011Fimiz iyili\u011Fi bize kaybettirirler.",
        "William Shakespeare": "William Shakespeare",
        "It is not in the stars to hold our destiny, but in ourselves.": "Kaderimiz y\u0131ld\u0131zlarda de\u011Fil, kendi i\xE7imizdedir.",
        "Wisely and slow; they stumble that run fast.": "Ak\u0131ll\u0131ca ve yava\u015F git; h\u0131zl\u0131 ko\u015Fan t\xF6kezler.",
        "The man who is prepared has his battle half fought.": "Haz\u0131rl\u0131kl\u0131 olan, sava\u015F\u0131n\u0131n yar\u0131s\u0131n\u0131 kazanm\u0131\u015Ft\u0131r.",
        "Miguel de Cervantes": "Miguel de Cervantes",
        "Diligence is the mother of good fortune.": "\xC7al\u0131\u015Fkanl\u0131k, talihin anas\u0131d\u0131r.",
        "Follow your own star.": "Kendi y\u0131ld\u0131z\u0131n\u0131n pe\u015Finden git.",
        "Dante Alighieri": "Dante Alighieri",
        "There is nothing like a dream to create the future.": "Gelece\u011Fi kurmak i\xE7in bir hayalden daha g\xFC\xE7l\xFC bir \u015Fey yoktur.",
        "Victor Hugo": "Victor Hugo",
        "Perseverance is the secret of all triumphs.": "Sebat, b\xFCt\xFCn zaferlerin s\u0131rr\u0131d\u0131r.",
        "Beauty will save the world.": "D\xFCnyay\u0131 g\xFCzellik kurtaracak.",
        "Fyodor Dostoyevsky": "Dostoyevski",
        "To live without hope is to cease to live.": "Umutsuz ya\u015Famak, ya\u015Famaktan vazge\xE7mektir.",
        "If you want to work on your art, work on your life.": "Sanat\u0131n\u0131n \xFCzerinde \xE7al\u0131\u015Fmak istiyorsan, hayat\u0131n\u0131n \xFCzerinde \xE7al\u0131\u015F.",
        "Anton Chekhov": "Anton \xC7ehov",
        "A thousand words leave not the same deep mark as a single deed.": "Bin s\xF6z, tek bir eylemin b\u0131rakt\u0131\u011F\u0131 derin izi b\u0131rakmaz.",
        "Henrik Ibsen": "Henrik Ibsen",
        "Fill the unforgiving minute with sixty seconds' worth of distance run.": "Affetmeyen dakikay\u0131, altm\u0131\u015F saniyelik ko\u015Fulmu\u015F yolla doldur.",
        "Rudyard Kipling": "Rudyard Kipling",
        "Mark Twain": "Mark Twain",
        "Twenty years from now you will be more disappointed by the things you didn't do than by the ones you did.": "Yirmi y\u0131l sonra, yapt\u0131klar\u0131ndan \xE7ok yapmad\u0131klar\u0131na hay\u0131flanacaks\u0131n.",
        "Continuous improvement is better than delayed perfection.": "S\xFCrekli geli\u015Fim, ertelenmi\u015F m\xFCkemmellikten iyidir.",
        "Either write something worth reading or do something worth writing.": "Ya okunmaya de\u011Fer bir \u015Fey yaz ya da yaz\u0131lmaya de\u011Fer bir \u015Fey yap.",
        "By failing to prepare, you are preparing to fail.": "Haz\u0131rlanmay\u0131 ihmal ederek, ba\u015Far\u0131s\u0131zl\u0131\u011Fa haz\u0131rlan\u0131rs\u0131n.",
        "Little strokes fell great oaks.": "K\xFC\xE7\xFCk darbeler, b\xFCy\xFCk me\u015Feleri devirir.",
        "Theodore Roosevelt": "Theodore Roosevelt",
        "The credit belongs to the one who is actually in the arena, whose face is marred by dust and sweat.": "\u015Eeref, ger\xE7ekten arenada olan\u0131n; y\xFCz\xFC tozla ve terle kaplanan\u0131nd\u0131r.",
        "Believe you can and you are halfway there.": "Yapabilece\u011Fine inan; yolun yar\u0131s\u0131n\u0131 gitmi\u015F olursun.",
        "The most effective way to do it is to do it.": "Bir i\u015Fi yapman\u0131n en etkili yolu, onu yapmakt\u0131r.",
        "Amelia Earhart": "Amelia Earhart",
        "Life is either a daring adventure or nothing at all.": "Hayat ya cesur bir macerad\u0131r ya da hi\xE7bir \u015Fey.",
        "Helen Keller": "Helen Keller",
        "Alone we can do so little; together we can do so much.": "Tek ba\u015F\u0131m\u0131za \xE7ok az \u015Fey yapabiliriz; birlikte \xE7ok \u015Fey ba\u015Far\u0131r\u0131z.",
        "A person who never made a mistake never tried anything new.": "Hi\xE7 hata yapmam\u0131\u015F biri, hi\xE7 yeni bir \u015Fey denememi\u015Ftir.",
        "The only source of knowledge is experience.": "Bilginin tek kayna\u011F\u0131 deneyimdir.",
        "Strive not to be a success, but rather to be of value.": "Ba\u015Far\u0131l\u0131 olmaya de\u011Fil, de\u011Ferli olmaya \xE7al\u0131\u015F.",
        "What we know is a drop; what we don't know is an ocean.": "Bildi\u011Fimiz bir damla, bilmedi\u011Fimiz bir okyanustur.",
        "If I have made any valuable discoveries, it has been owing more to patient attention than to any other talent.": "De\u011Ferli ke\u015Fifler yapt\u0131ysam, bu herhangi bir yetenekten \xE7ok sab\u0131rl\u0131 bir dikkat sayesinde olmu\u015Ftur.",
        "I was taught that the way of progress was neither swift nor easy.": "Bana ilerlemenin yolunun ne h\u0131zl\u0131 ne de kolay oldu\u011Fu \xF6\u011Fretildi.",
        "We must have perseverance and above all confidence in ourselves.": "Azme ve her \u015Feyden \xF6nce kendimize g\xFCvene sahip olmal\u0131y\u0131z.",
        "Let me tell you the secret that has led me to my goal: my strength lies solely in my tenacity.": "Sana beni hedefime ula\u015Ft\u0131ran s\u0131rr\u0131 s\xF6yleyeyim: g\xFCc\xFCm yaln\u0131zca azmimde yatar.",
        "Truth is the daughter of time, and I feel no shame in being her midwife.": "Hakikat zaman\u0131n k\u0131z\u0131d\u0131r ve onun ebesi olmaktan utan\xE7 duymuyorum.",
        "Johannes Kepler": "Johannes Kepler",
        "The heart has its reasons which reason knows nothing of.": "Kalbin, akl\u0131n hi\xE7 bilmedi\u011Fi kendi gerek\xE7eleri vard\u0131r.",
        "Blaise Pascal": "Blaise Pascal",
        "Truth is sought for its own sake.": "Hakikat, kendisi i\xE7in aran\u0131r.",
        "Ibn al-Haytham": "\u0130bn\xFC'l-Heysem",
        "Seek knowledge from the cradle to the grave.": "Be\u015Fikten mezara kadar ilim pe\u015Finde ko\u015F.",
        "Islamic tradition": "\u0130slam gelene\u011Fi",
        "If we all worked on the assumption that what is accepted as true is really true, there would be little hope of advance.": "Hepimiz do\u011Fru kabul edilenin ger\xE7ekten do\u011Fru oldu\u011Funu varsaysayd\u0131k, ilerleme umudu pek kalmazd\u0131.",
        "Orville Wright": "Orville Wright",
        "It is possible to fly without motors, but not without knowledge and skill.": "Motorsuz u\xE7mak m\xFCmk\xFCnd\xFCr, ama bilgisiz ve beceri olmadan asla.",
        "Wilbur Wright": "Wilbur Wright",
        "That brain of mine is something more than merely mortal, as time will show.": "Benim bu zihnim salt faniden fazlas\u0131d\u0131r; zaman bunu g\xF6sterecek.",
        "Ada Lovelace": "Ada Lovelace",
        "However difficult life may seem, there is always something you can do and succeed at.": "Hayat ne kadar zor g\xF6r\xFCn\xFCrse g\xF6r\xFCns\xFCn, her zaman yapabilece\u011Fin ve ba\u015Farabilece\u011Fin bir \u015Fey vard\u0131r.",
        "Stephen Hawking": "Stephen Hawking",
        "Look up at the stars and not down at your feet.": "Ayaklar\u0131na de\u011Fil, yukar\u0131ya, y\u0131ld\u0131zlara bak.",
        "The first principle is that you must not fool yourself \u2014 and you are the easiest person to fool.": "\u0130lk ilke, kendini kand\u0131rmamand\u0131r \u2014 ve kand\u0131rmas\u0131 en kolay ki\u015Fi sensin.",
        "Richard Feynman": "Richard Feynman",
        "What I cannot create, I do not understand.": "Yaratamad\u0131\u011F\u0131m \u015Feyi anlam\u0131\u015F say\u0131lmam.",
        "Somewhere, something incredible is waiting to be known.": "Bir yerlerde, inan\u0131lmaz bir \u015Fey bilinmeyi bekliyor.",
        "Carl Sagan": "Carl Sagan",
        "Imagination will often carry us to worlds that never were. But without it we go nowhere.": "Hayal g\xFCc\xFC bizi \xE7o\u011Fu zaman hi\xE7 var olmam\u0131\u015F d\xFCnyalara ta\u015F\u0131r. Ama o olmadan hi\xE7bir yere gidemeyiz.",
        "Ninety-nine percent of the failures come from people who have the habit of making excuses.": "Ba\u015Far\u0131s\u0131zl\u0131klar\u0131n y\xFCzde doksan dokuzu, bahane \xFCretme al\u0131\u015Fkanl\u0131\u011F\u0131 olan insanlardan gelir.",
        "George Washington Carver": "George Washington Carver",
        "I attribute my success to this: I never gave or took any excuse.": "Ba\u015Far\u0131m\u0131 \u015Funa bor\xE7luyum: hi\xE7bir zaman bahane sunmad\u0131m, bahane de kabul etmedim.",
        "Florence Nightingale": "Florence Nightingale",
        "Be alone; that is the secret of invention.": "Yaln\u0131z kal; bulu\u015Fun s\u0131rr\u0131 budur.",
        "You cannot teach a man anything; you can only help him find it within himself.": "Bir insana hi\xE7bir \u015Fey \xF6\u011Fretemezsin; yaln\u0131zca onu kendi i\xE7inde bulmas\u0131na yard\u0131m edebilirsin.",
        "Act as if what you do makes a difference. It does.": "Yapt\u0131\u011F\u0131n \u015Fey fark yarat\u0131yormu\u015F gibi davran. \xC7\xFCnk\xFC yarat\u0131yor.",
        "William James": "William James",
        "The greatest weapon against stress is our ability to choose one thought over another.": "Strese kar\u015F\u0131 en b\xFCy\xFCk silah\u0131m\u0131z, bir d\xFC\u015F\xFCnceyi di\u011Ferine tercih edebilme yetene\u011Fimizdir.",
        "Nothing is so fatiguing as the eternal hanging on of an uncompleted task.": "Hi\xE7bir \u015Fey, yar\u0131m kalm\u0131\u015F bir i\u015Fin \xFCzerinde as\u0131l\u0131 durmas\u0131 kadar yorucu de\u011Fildir.",
        "The art of being wise is the art of knowing what to overlook.": "Bilge olma sanat\u0131, neyi g\xF6rmezden gelece\u011Fini bilme sanat\u0131d\u0131r.",
        "Between stimulus and response there is a space. In that space is our power to choose.": "Uyar\u0131c\u0131 ile tepki aras\u0131nda bir bo\u015Fluk vard\u0131r. Se\xE7me g\xFCc\xFCm\xFCz o bo\u015Fluktad\u0131r.",
        "Viktor Frankl": "Viktor Frankl",
        "When we are no longer able to change a situation, we are challenged to change ourselves.": "Bir durumu art\u0131k de\u011Fi\u015Ftiremedi\u011Fimizde, kendimizi de\u011Fi\u015Ftirmekle s\u0131nan\u0131r\u0131z.",
        "Everything can be taken from a man but one thing: the freedom to choose one's attitude.": "\u0130nsandan her \u015Fey al\u0131nabilir, bir \u015Fey hari\xE7: tutumunu se\xE7me \xF6zg\xFCrl\xFC\u011F\xFC.",
        "Who looks outside, dreams; who looks inside, awakes.": "D\u0131\u015Far\u0131ya bakan r\xFCya g\xF6r\xFCr; i\xE7eriye bakan uyan\u0131r.",
        "Carl Jung": "Carl Jung",
        "I am not what happened to me, I am what I choose to become.": "Ben ba\u015F\u0131ma gelenler de\u011Filim; olmay\u0131 se\xE7ti\u011Fim ki\u015Fiyim.",
        "Until you make the unconscious conscious, it will direct your life and you will call it fate.": "Bilin\xE7d\u0131\u015F\u0131n\u0131 bilin\xE7li k\u0131lmad\u0131k\xE7a, o senin hayat\u0131n\u0131 y\xF6netir ve sen buna kader dersin.",
        "Do not spoil what you have by desiring what you have not.": "Sahip olmad\u0131\u011F\u0131n\u0131 arzulayarak sahip oldu\u011Funu berbat etme.",
        "Epicurus": "Epikuros",
        "Not what we have but what we enjoy constitutes our abundance.": "Zenginli\u011Fimizi sahip olduklar\u0131m\u0131z de\u011Fil, tad\u0131n\u0131 \xE7\u0131kard\u0131klar\u0131m\u0131z olu\u015Fturur.",
        "Life can only be understood backwards; but it must be lived forwards.": "Hayat ancak geriye do\u011Fru anla\u015F\u0131labilir; ama ileriye do\u011Fru ya\u015Fanmak zorundad\u0131r.",
        "S\xF8ren Kierkegaard": "S\xF8ren Kierkegaard",
        "To dare is to lose one's footing momentarily. Not to dare is to lose oneself.": "Cesaret etmek bir an dengeni kaybetmektir. Cesaret etmemek ise kendini kaybetmektir.",
        "Ordinary people think merely of spending time; a man of talent tries to use it.": "S\u0131radan insanlar zaman\u0131 yaln\u0131zca ge\xE7irmeyi d\xFC\u015F\xFCn\xFCr; yetenekli insan onu kullanmaya \xE7al\u0131\u015F\u0131r.",
        "Arthur Schopenhauer": "Arthur Schopenhauer",
        "Health is not everything, but without health everything is nothing.": "Sa\u011Fl\u0131k her \u015Fey de\u011Fildir, ama sa\u011Fl\u0131k olmadan her \u015Fey hi\xE7tir.",
        "The greatest thing in the world is to know how to belong to oneself.": "D\xFCnyadaki en b\xFCy\xFCk \u015Fey, kendine ait olmay\u0131 bilmektir.",
        "Michel de Montaigne": "Michel de Montaigne",
        "He who fears he shall suffer, already suffers what he fears.": "Ac\u0131 \xE7ekmekten korkan, korktu\u011Fu ac\u0131y\u0131 \u015Fimdiden \xE7ekiyordur.",
        "All of humanity's problems stem from man's inability to sit quietly in a room alone.": "\u0130nsanl\u0131\u011F\u0131n b\xFCt\xFCn sorunlar\u0131, insan\u0131n bir odada tek ba\u015F\u0131na sessizce oturamamas\u0131ndan kaynaklan\u0131r.",
        "It is not because things are difficult that we do not dare; it is because we do not dare that things are difficult.": "\u0130\u015Fler zor oldu\u011Fu i\xE7in cesaret edemiyor de\u011Filiz; cesaret edemedi\u011Fimiz i\xE7in i\u015Fler zor.",
        "Patience is a tree whose root is bitter, but its fruit is sweet.": "Sab\u0131r, k\xF6k\xFC ac\u0131 ama meyvesi tatl\u0131 bir a\u011Fa\xE7t\u0131r.",
        "Persian proverb": "Fars atas\xF6z\xFC",
        "This too shall pass.": "Bu da ge\xE7er.",
        "Sunshine all the time makes a desert.": "Hep g\xFCne\u015F a\xE7arsa, oras\u0131 \xE7\xF6le d\xF6ner.",
        "Arabic proverb": "Arap atas\xF6z\xFC",
        "He who wants honey must endure the sting of bees.": "Bal isteyen, ar\u0131n\u0131n i\u011Fnesine katlan\u0131r.",
        "Call on God, but row away from the rocks.": "Tanr\u0131'ya yakar, ama kayal\u0131klardan uza\u011Fa k\xFCrek \xE7ek.",
        "Indian proverb": "Hint atas\xF6z\xFC",
        "Even a sheet of paper is lighter when lifted together.": "Bir ka\u011F\u0131t yapra\u011F\u0131 bile birlikte kald\u0131r\u0131nca hafifler.",
        "Korean proverb": "Kore atas\xF6z\xFC",
        "At the end of hardship comes happiness.": "Zorlu\u011Fun sonunda mutluluk gelir.",
        "Without effort, you cannot even pull a fish out of the pond.": "Emek vermeden g\xF6lden bal\u0131k bile \xE7\u0131karamazs\u0131n.",
        "Russian proverb": "Rus atas\xF6z\xFC",
        "Measure seven times, cut once.": "Yedi kez \xF6l\xE7, bir kez kes.",
        "Beginning is easy; persisting is an art.": "Ba\u015Flamak kolayd\u0131r; s\xFCrd\xFCrmek sanatt\u0131r.",
        "German proverb": "Alman atas\xF6z\xFC",
        "The morning hour has gold in its mouth.": "Sabah\u0131n saati, a\u011Fz\u0131nda alt\u0131n ta\u015F\u0131r.",
        "Between saying and doing lies the sea.": "S\xF6ylemekle yapmak aras\u0131nda bir deniz vard\u0131r.",
        "Italian proverb": "\u0130talyan atas\xF6z\xFC",
        "He who goes slowly goes safely and goes far.": "Yava\u015F giden, sa\u011Flam gider ve uza\u011Fa var\u0131r.",
        "You'll never plough a field by turning it over in your mind.": "Tarlay\u0131 kafanda evirip \xE7evirerek s\xFCremezsin.",
        "Irish proverb": "\u0130rlanda atas\xF6z\xFC",
        "Those who wish to sing always find a song.": "\u015Eark\u0131 s\xF6ylemek isteyen, her zaman bir \u015Fark\u0131 bulur.",
        "Swedish proverb": "\u0130sve\xE7 atas\xF6z\xFC",
        "A society grows great when old men plant trees whose shade they know they shall never sit in.": "Bir toplum, ya\u015Fl\u0131lar\u0131n g\xF6lgesinde asla oturamayacaklar\u0131n\u0131 bildikleri a\u011Fa\xE7lar\u0131 dikti\u011Finde y\xFCcelir.",
        "Greek proverb": "Yunan atas\xF6z\xFC",
        "Soft water strikes the hard stone until it bores through.": "Yumu\u015Fak su, sert ta\u015Fa vura vura onu deler.",
        "Portuguese proverb": "Portekiz atas\xF6z\xFC",
        "They tried to bury us; they didn't know we were seeds.": "Bizi g\xF6mmeye \xE7al\u0131\u015Ft\u0131lar; tohum oldu\u011Fumuzu bilmiyorlard\u0131.",
        "Mexican proverb": "Meksika atas\xF6z\xFC",
        "The soul would have no rainbow if the eyes had no tears.": "G\xF6zlerde ya\u015F olmasayd\u0131, ruhta g\xF6kku\u015Fa\u011F\u0131 olmazd\u0131.",
        "Native American proverb": "K\u0131z\u0131lderili atas\xF6z\xFC",
        "Before enlightenment, chop wood, carry water. After enlightenment, chop wood, carry water.": "Ayd\u0131nlanmadan \xF6nce odun k\u0131r, su ta\u015F\u0131. Ayd\u0131nland\u0131ktan sonra odun k\u0131r, su ta\u015F\u0131.",
        "Zen saying": "Zen deyi\u015Fi",
        "This is the day the Lord has made; let us rejoice and be glad in it.": "Bug\xFCn Rab'bin yaratt\u0131\u011F\u0131 g\xFCnd\xFCr; onda sevinelim, co\u015Fal\u0131m.",
        "Psalm 118:24": "Mezmur 118:24",
        "Weeping may endure for a night, but joy comes in the morning.": "A\u011Flay\u0131\u015F bir gece s\xFCrebilir, ama sabahla sevin\xE7 gelir.",
        "Psalm 30:5": "Mezmur 30:5",
        "Be still, and know that I am God.": "Sakin olun ve bilin ki Tanr\u0131 benim.",
        "Psalm 46:10": "Mezmur 46:10",
        "Commit your way to the Lord; trust in Him, and He will act.": "Yolunu Rab'be emanet et; O'na g\xFCven, O gerekeni yapar.",
        "Psalm 37:5": "Mezmur 37:5",
        "The soul of the diligent shall be made rich.": "\xC7al\u0131\u015Fkan\u0131n can\u0131 zenginli\u011Fe kavu\u015Fur.",
        "Proverbs 13:4": "\xD6zdeyi\u015Fler 13:4",
        "A righteous man falls seven times, and rises again.": "Do\u011Fru insan yedi kez d\xFC\u015Fse de yine kalkar.",
        "Proverbs 24:16": "\xD6zdeyi\u015Fler 24:16",
        "To everything there is a season, and a time to every purpose under heaven.": "Her \u015Feyin bir mevsimi, g\xF6\u011F\xFCn alt\u0131ndaki her amac\u0131n bir zaman\u0131 vard\u0131r.",
        "Ecclesiastes 3:1": "Vaiz 3:1",
        "Whoever watches the wind will not plant; whoever looks at the clouds will not reap.": "R\xFCzgar\u0131 g\xF6zleyen ekemez; bulutlara bakan bi\xE7emez.",
        "Ecclesiastes 11:4": "Vaiz 11:4",
        "Faith by itself, if it does not have works, is dead.": "\u0130man, eylemleri yoksa, tek ba\u015F\u0131na \xF6l\xFCd\xFCr.",
        "James 2:17": "Yakup 2:17",
        "Let us not grow weary in doing good, for in due season we shall reap.": "\u0130yilik yapmaktan usanmayal\u0131m; vakti gelince bi\xE7eriz.",
        "Galatians 6:9": "Galatyal\u0131lar 6:9",
        "Those who wait on the Lord shall renew their strength; they shall mount up with wings like eagles.": "Rab'bi bekleyenler g\xFC\xE7lerini tazeler; kartal kanatlar\u0131yla y\xFCkselirler.",
        "Isaiah 40:31": "Ye\u015Faya 40:31",
        "Go, sit in your cell, and your cell will teach you everything.": "Git, h\xFCcrende otur; h\xFCcren sana her \u015Feyi \xF6\u011Fretecektir.",
        "Desert Fathers": "\xC7\xF6l Babalar\u0131",
        "Start by doing what's necessary; then do what's possible; and suddenly you are doing the impossible.": "\xD6nce gerekli olan\u0131 yap; sonra m\xFCmk\xFCn olan\u0131; ve bir bakm\u0131\u015Fs\u0131n, imkans\u0131z\u0131 yap\u0131yorsun.",
        "St. Francis of Assisi": "Assisili Aziz Francesco",
        "First keep peace with yourself; then you can also bring peace to others.": "\xD6nce kendinle bar\u0131\u015F i\xE7inde ol; ancak o zaman ba\u015Fkalar\u0131na da bar\u0131\u015F g\xF6t\xFCrebilirsin.",
        "Thomas \xE0 Kempis": "Thomas \xE0 Kempis",
        "Faith is to believe what you do not see; the reward of this faith is to see what you believe.": "\u0130man, g\xF6rmedi\u011Fine inanmakt\u0131r; bu iman\u0131n \xF6d\xFCl\xFC ise inand\u0131\u011F\u0131n\u0131 g\xF6rmektir.",
        "St. Augustine": "Aziz Augustinus",
        "A moment of patience in a moment of anger saves a thousand moments of regret.": "\xD6fke an\u0131ndaki bir anl\u0131k sab\u0131r, bin anl\u0131k pi\u015Fmanl\u0131ktan kurtar\u0131r.",
        "Ibn Qayyim al-Jawziyya": "\u0130bn Kayyim el-Cevziyye",
        "Do not ruin your happiness with worry, and do not ruin your mind with pessimism.": "Mutlulu\u011Funu kayg\u0131yla, zihnini karamsarl\u0131kla harap etme.",
        "If you do not occupy yourself with truth, falsehood will occupy you.": "Kendini hakikatle me\u015Fgul etmezsen, bat\u0131l seni me\u015Fgul eder.",
        "Imam Shafi'i": "\u0130mam \u015Eafii",
        "Flowing water stays pure; standing water grows stale.": "Akan su temiz kal\u0131r; duran su bozulur.",
        "Do not let your difficulties fill you with anxiety; it is only in the darkest nights that stars shine more brightly.": "Zorluklar\u0131n seni kayg\u0131yla doldurmas\u0131n; y\u0131ld\u0131zlar en \xE7ok en karanl\u0131k gecelerde parlar.",
        "Believe you can and you're halfway there.": "Yapabilece\u011Fine inan; yolun yar\u0131s\u0131 tamamd\u0131r.",
        "If you're going through hell, keep going.": "Cehennemden ge\xE7iyorsan, y\xFCr\xFCmeye devam et.",
        "Courage is what it takes to stand up and speak; courage is also what it takes to sit down and listen.": "Cesaret, aya\u011Fa kalk\u0131p konu\u015Fmak i\xE7in gerekir; oturup dinlemek i\xE7in de.",
        "Opportunity is missed by most people because it is dressed in overalls and looks like work.": "\xC7o\u011Fu insan f\u0131rsat\u0131 ka\xE7\u0131r\u0131r, \xE7\xFCnk\xFC f\u0131rsat tulum giyer ve i\u015F gibi g\xF6r\xFCn\xFCr.",
        "Our greatest weakness lies in giving up. The most certain way to succeed is always to try just one more time.": "En b\xFCy\xFCk zay\u0131fl\u0131\u011F\u0131m\u0131z pes etmektir. Ba\u015Farman\u0131n en kesin yolu, her zaman bir kez daha denemektir.",
        "Whether you think you can, or you think you can't \u2014 you're right.": "\u0130ster yapabilece\u011Fini d\xFC\u015F\xFCn, ister yapamayaca\u011F\u0131n\u0131 \u2014 hakl\u0131s\u0131n.",
        "Henry Ford": "Henry Ford",
        "The way to get started is to quit talking and begin doing.": "Ba\u015Flaman\u0131n yolu, konu\u015Fmay\u0131 b\u0131rak\u0131p yapmaya koyulmakt\u0131r.",
        "Walt Disney": "Walt Disney",
        "The future belongs to those who believe in the beauty of their dreams.": "Gelecek, hayallerinin g\xFCzelli\u011Fine inananlar\u0131nd\u0131r.",
        "Eleanor Roosevelt": "Eleanor Roosevelt",
        "Do one thing every day that scares you.": "Her g\xFCn seni korkutan bir \u015Fey yap.",
        "Don't count the days; make the days count.": "G\xFCnleri sayma; g\xFCnleri de\u011Ferli k\u0131l.",
        "Muhammad Ali": "Muhammed Ali",
        "Do not pray for an easy life; pray for the strength to endure a difficult one.": "Kolay bir hayat i\xE7in dua etme; zor bir hayata dayanacak g\xFC\xE7 i\xE7in dua et.",
        "Bruce Lee": "Bruce Lee",
        "Be water, my friend.": "Su gibi ol, dostum.",
        "Stay hungry, stay foolish.": "A\xE7 kal, ak\u0131ls\u0131z kal.",
        "Steve Jobs": "Steve Jobs",
        "The only way to do great work is to love what you do.": "Harika i\u015Fler yapman\u0131n tek yolu, yapt\u0131\u011F\u0131n i\u015Fi sevmektir.",
        "This browser doesn't support background notifications. On iPhone/iPad, add the site to your Home Screen and open it from there.": "Bu taray\u0131c\u0131 arka plan bildirimlerini desteklemiyor. iPhone/iPad i\xE7in siteyi ana ekrana ekleyip oradan a\xE7.",
        "The background notification server isn't set up yet.": "Arka plan bildirim sunucusu hen\xFCz kurulmad\u0131.",
        "Sign in to your account to get notifications while the site is closed.": "Site kapal\u0131yken bildirim almak i\xE7in \xFCyeli\u011Fine giri\u015F yap.",
        "Sign in to your account to change notification settings.": "Bildirim ayarlar\u0131n\u0131 de\u011Fi\u015Ftirmek i\xE7in \xFCyeli\u011Fine giri\u015F yap.",
        "Couldn't reach the notification server. Check your connection and try again.": "Bildirim sunucusuna ula\u015F\u0131lamad\u0131. Ba\u011Flant\u0131n\u0131 kontrol edip tekrar dene.",
        "Your session needs refreshing. Sign out and sign in again.": "Oturumun yenilenmeli. \xC7\u0131k\u0131\u015F yap\u0131p tekrar giri\u015F yap.",
        "Background notifications aren't ready yet. The notification setup on the server needs to be completed.": "Arka plan bildirim altyap\u0131s\u0131 haz\u0131r de\u011Fil. Sunucudaki bildirim kurulumunun tamamlanmas\u0131 gerekiyor.",
        "Couldn't verify the notification registration for this account. Try signing in again.": "Bu \xFCyelik i\xE7in bildirim kayd\u0131 do\u011Frulanamad\u0131. Yeniden giri\u015F yapmay\u0131 dene.",
        "Couldn't save the notification setting to the server. Try again.": "Bildirim ayar\u0131 sunucuya kaydedilemedi. Tekrar dene.",
        "Choose a valid time for all six notifications.": "Alt\u0131 bildirim i\xE7in ge\xE7erli bir saat se\xE7.",
        "Choose a different time for each of the six notifications.": "Alt\u0131 bildirim i\xE7in birbirinden farkl\u0131 saatler se\xE7.",
        "The notification service couldn't start. Refresh the page and try again.": "Bildirim servisi haz\u0131rlanamad\u0131. Sayfay\u0131 yenileyip tekrar dene.",
        "Couldn't verify notification status.": "Bildirim durumu do\u011Frulanamad\u0131.",
        "Notification permission wasn't granted. You can allow it in your browser's site settings.": "Bildirim izni verilmedi. Taray\u0131c\u0131n\u0131n site ayarlar\u0131ndan izin verebilirsin.",
        "Couldn't close the previous device subscription. Refresh the page and try again.": "\xD6nceki cihaz aboneli\u011Fi kapat\u0131lamad\u0131. Sayfay\u0131 yenileyip tekrar dene.",
        "The signed-in account changed. Turn notifications on again from the account you're using.": "\xDCyelik oturumu de\u011Fi\u015Fti. Bildirimleri a\xE7\u0131k olan \xFCyelikte yeniden etkinle\u015Ftir.",
        "Notifications couldn't be stopped yet. Check your connection or turn off notification permission in your browser's site settings.": "Bildirimler hen\xFCz durdurulamad\u0131. Ba\u011Flant\u0131y\u0131 kontrol et veya taray\u0131c\u0131n\u0131n site bildirim iznini kapat.",
        "Notifications are off on this device, but the server record couldn't be cleared. Try turning them off again when you're back online.": "Bu cihazdaki bildirimler kapat\u0131ld\u0131; sunucu kayd\u0131 temizlenemedi. Ba\u011Flant\u0131 gelince tekrar kapatmay\u0131 dene.",
        "Server notifications are off, but the browser subscription couldn't be removed. Refresh the page and try again.": "Sunucu bildirimleri kapat\u0131ld\u0131; taray\u0131c\u0131 aboneli\u011Fi kald\u0131r\u0131lamad\u0131. Sayfay\u0131 yenileyip tekrar dene.",
        "The server subscription wasn't found. Turn background notifications on again.": "Sunucu aboneli\u011Fi bulunamad\u0131. Arka plan bildirimlerini yeniden a\xE7.",
        "Course lessons are currently available in Turkish.": "Kurs dersleri \u015Fu an T\xFCrk\xE7e olarak sunuluyor.",
        "This browser can't save your progress right now. If you close the page, changes from this session may be lost.": "Bu taray\u0131c\u0131 \u015Fu an ilerlemeyi kaydedemiyor. Sayfay\u0131 kapat\u0131rsan bu oturumdaki de\u011Fi\u015Fiklikler kaybolabilir.",
        "Your progress and optional notes are stored in this browser. They are not sent to the cloud and will be lost if browser data is cleared. On a shared device, you may prefer not to leave personal notes.": "\u0130lerlemen ve iste\u011Fe ba\u011Fl\u0131 notlar\u0131n bu taray\u0131c\u0131da saklan\u0131r. Buluta g\xF6nderilmez; taray\u0131c\u0131 verileri silinirse kaybolur. Ortak cihaz kullan\u0131yorsan ki\u015Fisel not b\u0131rakmamay\u0131 se\xE7ebilirsin.",
        "ODA / Guided courses": "ODA / Rehberli kurslar",
        "Even if you're afraid,": "Korksan da",
        "you can still begin.": "ba\u015Flayabilirsin.",
        "Sometimes a quote gives you courage. Sometimes you need to see the next step together. Pick a topic and move at your own pace with short lessons.": "Bazen bir s\xF6z cesaret verir. Bazen de s\u0131radaki ad\u0131m\u0131 birlikte g\xF6rmek gerekir. Kendine bir konu se\xE7; k\u0131sa derslerle, kendi h\u0131z\u0131nda ilerle.",
        "Understand": "Anla",
        "Try": "Dene",
        "Reinforce": "Peki\u015Ftir",
        "{courses} courses \xB7 {lessons} lessons": "{courses} kurs \xB7 {lessons} ders",
        "Content based on {count} scientific publications": "{count} bilimsel yay\u0131na dayanan i\xE7erik",
        "Continue the course you started": "Ba\u015Flad\u0131\u011F\u0131n kursa devam et",
        "Where you left off": "Kald\u0131\u011F\u0131n yerden",
        "Lesson {number}": "Ders {number}",
        "{done}/{total} lessons completed": "{done}/{total} ders tamamland\u0131",
        "Explore the other paths too": "Di\u011Fer yollar\u0131 da ke\u015Ffet",
        "Which topic feels close to you today?": "Bug\xFCn hangi konu sana yak\u0131n?",
        "Pick a topic. Start with one small step.": "Bir konu se\xE7. K\xFC\xE7\xFCk bir ad\u0131mla ba\u015Fla.",
        "{lessons} lessons \xB7 {minutes} min": "{lessons} ders \xB7 {minutes} dk",
        "Completed \xB7 review again": "Tamamland\u0131 \xB7 tekrar bak",
        "{done}/{total} completed \xB7 continue": "{done}/{total} tamamland\u0131 \xB7 devam et",
        "Start course": "Kursa ba\u015Fla",
        "{title} progress": "{title} ilerlemesi",
        "If you're curious": "Merak edersen",
        "What are these lessons based on?": "Bu dersler neye dayan\u0131yor?",
        "Six scientific publications were reviewed before the lessons were written. Research findings were adapted into original daily exercises. ODA courses themselves have not been clinically tested; they are for education and personal practice.": "Dersler yaz\u0131lmadan \xF6nce alt\u0131 bilimsel yay\u0131n incelendi. Ara\u015Ft\u0131rma bulgular\u0131, \xF6zg\xFCn g\xFCnl\xFCk al\u0131\u015Ft\u0131rmalara uyarland\u0131. ODA kurslar\u0131n\u0131n kendisi klinik olarak s\u0131nanmad\u0131; e\u011Fitim ve ki\u015Fisel \xE7al\u0131\u015Fma i\xE7indir.",
        "Read the publication": "Yay\u0131n\u0131 oku",
        "All courses": "T\xFCm kurslar",
        "Lesson {number} / {total}": "Ders {number} / {total}",
        "About {minutes} minutes \xB7 at your own pace": "Yakla\u015F\u0131k {minutes} dakika \xB7 kendi h\u0131z\u0131nda",
        "Lesson order": "Ders s\u0131ras\u0131",
        "Lesson {number}: {title}, completed": "Ders {number}: {title}, tamamland\u0131",
        "Lesson {number}: {title}, complete the previous lesson first": "Ders {number}: {title}, \xF6nce bir \xF6nceki dersi tamamla",
        "Lesson {number}: {title}": "Ders {number}: {title}",
        "This lesson's small goal": "Bu dersin k\xFC\xE7\xFCk hedefi",
        "Let's try it together now. Check off each step after you try it. You can pause anytime.": "\u015Eimdi birlikte deneyelim. Her ad\u0131m\u0131 denedikten sonra i\u015Faretle. \u0130stedi\u011Fin zaman ara verebilirsin.",
        "Leaving a note is optional; you can keep your answer just for yourself.": "Not b\u0131rakmak iste\u011Fe ba\u011Fl\u0131; yan\u0131t\u0131n\u0131 yaln\u0131zca kendin i\xE7in tutabilirsin.",
        "A small note to myself\u2026": "Kendime k\xFC\xE7\xFCk bir not\u2026",
        "A quick check": "K\u0131sa bir kontrol",
        "Yes, this approach fits the goal of the lesson.": "Evet, bu yakla\u015F\u0131m dersin amac\u0131na uygun.",
        "Let's think about it once more.": "Bir kez daha d\xFC\u015F\xFCnelim.",
        "You can go back to the explanation and choose another answer.": "A\xE7\u0131klamaya d\xF6n\xFCp ba\u015Fka bir yan\u0131t se\xE7ebilirsin.",
        "Sources and limits of this lesson": "Bu dersin kaynaklar\u0131 ve s\u0131n\u0131rlar\u0131",
        "Scientific publication": "Bilimsel yay\u0131n",
        "Religious source": "Din\xEE kaynak",
        "Official health guidance": "Resm\xEE sa\u011Fl\u0131k rehberi",
        "Course completed": "Kurs tamamland\u0131",
        "Lesson completed": "Bu ders tamamland\u0131",
        "What you take with you: {outcome} You can reread the lessons whenever you like.": "Yan\u0131na alaca\u011F\u0131n \u015Fey: {outcome} Dersleri diledi\u011Finde tekrar okuyabilirsin.",
        "Go to the next lesson": "Sonraki derse ge\xE7",
        "Back to courses": "Kurslara d\xF6n",
        "To complete the lesson, check the three practice steps and choose the right answer to the question. A personal note is optional.": "Dersi tamamlamak i\xE7in \xFC\xE7 uygulama ad\u0131m\u0131n\u0131 i\u015Faretle ve sorunun uygun yan\u0131t\u0131n\u0131 se\xE7. Ki\u015Fisel not iste\u011Fe ba\u011Fl\u0131.",
        "Lesson completed. When you're ready, you can move to the next step.": "Ders tamamland\u0131. Haz\u0131r oldu\u011Funda sonraki ad\u0131ma ge\xE7ebilirsin.",
        "Complete lesson": "Dersi tamamla",
        "The operation was stopped.": "\u0130\u015Flem durduruldu.",
        "Your device couldn't free up enough memory for the AI. Close other tabs and try restarting the coach.": "Cihaz\u0131n yapay zek\xE2 i\xE7in yeterli bo\u015F belle\u011Fi sa\u011Flayamad\u0131. Di\u011Fer sekmeleri kapat\u0131p ko\xE7u yeniden ba\u015Flatmay\u0131 dene.",
        "The model files couldn't be loaded. Check your internet connection and your browser's free storage, then try again.": "Model dosyalar\u0131 y\xFCklenemedi. \u0130nternet ba\u011Flant\u0131n\u0131 ve taray\u0131c\u0131n\u0131n bo\u015F depolama alan\u0131n\u0131 kontrol edip yeniden dene.",
        "This browser or device doesn't support the AI engine. Try again in an up-to-date browser with WebGPU support.": "Bu taray\u0131c\u0131 veya cihaz yapay zek\xE2 motorunu desteklemiyor. G\xFCncel, WebGPU destekli bir taray\u0131c\u0131da tekrar dene.",
        "The AI couldn't finish its reply. Restart the coach and try again.": "Yapay zek\xE2 yan\u0131t\u0131 tamamlayamad\u0131. Ko\xE7u yeniden ba\u015Flat\u0131p tekrar dene.",
        "The live coach needs an up-to-date browser with WebGPU support.": "Canl\u0131 ko\xE7 i\xE7in WebGPU destekli g\xFCncel bir taray\u0131c\u0131 gerekiyor.",
        "Open the live coach from the site's secure HTTPS address.": "Canl\u0131 ko\xE7u sitenin g\xFCvenli HTTPS adresinden a\xE7.",
        "WebGPU isn't available in this browser. Try again with an up-to-date Chrome or Edge.": "Bu taray\u0131c\u0131da WebGPU kullan\u0131lam\u0131yor. G\xFCncel Chrome veya Edge ile tekrar dene.",
        "Couldn't access the graphics card. Turn on hardware acceleration in your browser and try again.": "Ekran kart\u0131na eri\u015Filemedi. Taray\u0131c\u0131n\u0131n donan\u0131m h\u0131zland\u0131rmas\u0131n\u0131 a\xE7\u0131p tekrar dene.",
        "The browser couldn't access the graphics card. Try another up-to-date browser with WebGPU support.": "Taray\u0131c\u0131 ekran kart\u0131na eri\u015Femedi. G\xFCncel ve WebGPU destekli ba\u015Fka bir taray\u0131c\u0131da dene.",
        "Write a message to send to the coach.": "Ko\xE7a g\xF6ndermek i\xE7in bir mesaj yaz.",
        "The AI engine stopped. Restart the coach and try again.": "Yapay zek\xE2 motoru durdu. Ko\xE7u yeniden ba\u015Flat\u0131p tekrar dene.",
        "Model ready.": "Model haz\u0131r.",
        "Checking device compatibility\u2026": "Cihaz uyumlulu\u011Fu kontrol ediliyor\u2026",
        "The live coach isn't supported on this device.": "Bu cihazda canl\u0131 ko\xE7 desteklenmiyor.",
        "The coach is ready. You can start talking.": "Ko\xE7 haz\u0131r. Konu\u015Fmaya ba\u015Flayabilirsin.",
        "Start the live coach first.": "\xD6nce canl\u0131 ko\xE7u ba\u015Flat.",
        "Wait for the previous reply to finish or stop it.": "\xD6nceki yan\u0131t\u0131n bitmesini bekle veya yan\u0131t\u0131 durdur.",
        "The coach couldn't create a reply this time. You can send your message again.": "Ko\xE7 bu kez bir yan\u0131t olu\u015Fturamad\u0131. Mesaj\u0131n\u0131 yeniden g\xF6nderebilirsin.",
        "Downloading and preparing the model \xB7 {percent}%": "Model indiriliyor ve haz\u0131rlan\u0131yor \xB7 %{percent}",
        "Daily check-in recorded. +D$50": "G\xFCnl\xFCk yoklama kaydedildi. +D$50",
        "Tab title blink is on.": "Sekme ba\u015Fl\u0131\u011F\u0131 yan\u0131p s\xF6nmesi a\xE7\u0131k.",
        "Tab title blink is off.": "Sekme ba\u015Fl\u0131\u011F\u0131 yan\u0131p s\xF6nmesi kapal\u0131.",
        "Screen edge pulse is on.": "Ekran kenar\u0131 \u0131\u015F\u0131k efekti a\xE7\u0131k.",
        "Screen edge pulse is off.": "Ekran kenar\u0131 \u0131\u015F\u0131k efekti kapal\u0131.",
        "Previewing the finish alert for 5 seconds.": "Biti\u015F uyar\u0131s\u0131 5 saniye boyunca \xF6nizleniyor.",
        "Plan saved. You know what to do when it gets hard.": "Plan kaydedildi. Zorla\u015Ft\u0131\u011F\u0131nda ne yapaca\u011F\u0131n\u0131 biliyorsun.",
        "Make it doable": "Yap\u0131labilir h\xE2le getir",
        "Your plan for today": "Bug\xFCnk\xFC plan\u0131n",
        "Thirty seconds now saves you from deciding again later.": "\u015Eimdi ay\u0131raca\u011F\u0131n otuz saniye, seni sonra yeniden karar vermekten kurtar\u0131r.",
        "1. How does this decision feel right now?": "1. Bu karar \u015Fu an sana nas\u0131l geliyor?",
        "Rewrite it smaller (optional)": "Daha k\xFC\xE7\xFCk h\xE2lini yaz (iste\u011Fe ba\u011Fl\u0131)",
        "2. What could stop you today?": "2. Bug\xFCn seni ne durdurabilir?",
        "e.g. I\u2019ll pick up my phone first": "\xF6rn. \xF6nce telefonu elime al\u0131r\u0131m",
        "3. If that happens, I will\u2026": "3. B\xF6yle olursa \u015Funu yapaca\u011F\u0131m\u2026",
        "e.g. put the phone in another room and start for two minutes": "\xF6rn. telefonu ba\u015Fka odaya b\u0131rak\u0131p iki dakikal\u0131\u011F\u0131na ba\u015Flar\u0131m",
        "Deciding in advance what you will do when the obstacle appears is one of the best-studied ways to follow through.": "Engel \xE7\u0131kt\u0131\u011F\u0131nda ne yapaca\u011F\u0131na \xF6nceden karar vermek, i\u015Fi sonuna g\xF6t\xFCrmenin en \xE7ok ara\u015Ft\u0131r\u0131lm\u0131\u015F yollar\u0131ndan biri.",
        "Save plan": "Plan\u0131 kaydet",
        "Make it real": "Ger\xE7e\u011Fe d\xF6n\xFC\u015Ft\xFCr",
        "Picturing a dream feels good, but on its own it can drain the energy to act. Name what\u2019s in the way, then take one small step.": "Bir hayali canland\u0131rmak iyi hissettirir ama tek ba\u015F\u0131na harekete ge\xE7me enerjisini t\xFCketebilir. \xD6n\xFCndeki engelin ad\u0131n\u0131 koy, sonra k\xFC\xE7\xFCk bir ad\u0131m at.",
        "What stands between you and this?": "Seninle bu hayal aras\u0131nda ne duruyor?",
        "Your next small step": "S\u0131radaki k\xFC\xE7\xFCk ad\u0131m\u0131n",
        "Make it today\u2019s decision": "Bug\xFCn\xFCn karar\u0131 olsun",
        "You already have a decision for today. Save this step for tomorrow.": "Bug\xFCn i\xE7in zaten bir karar\u0131n var. Bu ad\u0131m\u0131 yar\u0131n i\xE7in kaydet.",
        "Yesterday didn\u2019t happen. That\u2019s okay.": "D\xFCn olmad\u0131. Sorun de\u011Fil.",
        "Welcome back. Today is a clean page.": "Tekrar ho\u015F geldin. Bug\xFCn temiz bir sayfa.",
        "A new month, a clean page.": "Yeni bir ay, temiz bir sayfa.",
        "A new week, a clean page.": "Yeni bir hafta, temiz bir sayfa.",
        "Missing one day doesn\u2019t undo your progress. What matters is not missing twice. Choose the smallest version of today\u2019s decision.": "Bir g\xFCn\xFC ka\xE7\u0131rmak ilerlemeni silmez. \xD6nemli olan ikinci kez ka\xE7\u0131rmamak. Bug\xFCnk\xFC karar\u0131n en k\xFC\xE7\xFCk h\xE2lini se\xE7.",
        "No need to make up for the missed days. Go easy on yourself about the gap, and choose one small decision for today.": "Ka\xE7\u0131rd\u0131\u011F\u0131n g\xFCnleri telafi etmene gerek yok. Aradaki bo\u015Fluk i\xE7in kendine y\xFCklenme; bug\xFCn i\xE7in k\xFC\xE7\xFCk bir karar se\xE7.",
        "New beginnings make change easier to start. What do you want this period to be about? Begin with today\u2019s decision.": "Yeni ba\u015Flang\u0131\xE7lar de\u011Fi\u015Fmeyi kolayla\u015Ft\u0131r\u0131r. Bu d\xF6nem neyin d\xF6nemi olsun? Bug\xFCnk\xFC karar\u0131nla ba\u015Fla.",
        "Make it smaller": "K\xFC\xE7\xFClt",
        "Choose today\u2019s decision": "Bug\xFCn\xFCn karar\u0131n\u0131 se\xE7",
        "Your evidence starts today": "Kan\u0131tlar\u0131n bug\xFCn ba\u015Fl\u0131yor",
        "1 kept promise": "1 tutulan s\xF6z",
        "{n} kept promises": "{n} tutulan s\xF6z",
        "This week: {n} of 7 days": "Bu hafta: {n}/7 g\xFCn",
        "A simple start": "Sade bir ba\u015Flang\u0131\xE7",
        "For your first week you\u2019ll see only what matters most: one decision a day. The other tools open after {n} kept decisions.": "\u0130lk haftanda yaln\u0131zca en \xF6nemlisini g\xF6receksin: g\xFCnde tek bir karar. Di\u011Fer ara\xE7lar {n} karar\u0131 tuttuktan sonra a\xE7\u0131l\u0131r.",
        "Show everything now": "Hepsini \u015Fimdi g\xF6ster",
        "A little": "Biraz",
        "Not yet": "Hen\xFCz de\u011Fil",
        "Did you start something you had been putting off?": "Erteledi\u011Fin bir \u015Feye ba\u015Flad\u0131n m\u0131?",
        "Days since start: {n}": "Ba\u015Flang\u0131\xE7tan bu yana g\xFCn: {n}",
        "Decisions set: {n}": "Belirlenen karar: {n}",
        "Decisions kept: {n}": "Tutulan karar: {n}",
        "Plans made: {n}": "Yap\u0131lan plan: {n}",
        "Two-minute starts: {n}": "\u0130ki dakikal\u0131k ba\u015Flang\u0131\xE7: {n}",
        "Thank you. This helps us make ODA better.": "Te\u015Fekk\xFCrler. Bu, ODA'y\u0131 daha iyi yapmam\u0131za yard\u0131m ediyor.",
        "Two weeks in": "\u0130ki hafta oldu",
        "What helped, or what got in the way? (optional)": "Ne yard\u0131mc\u0131 oldu, ne engel oldu? (iste\u011Fe ba\u011Fl\u0131)",
        "Send to the ODA team": "ODA ekibine g\xF6nder",
        "Just save": "Sadece kaydet",
        "Sending opens your email app with your answer and a few usage numbers. Nothing is sent automatically.": "G\xF6nderince e-posta uygulaman, yan\u0131t\u0131n ve birka\xE7 kullan\u0131m say\u0131s\u0131yla a\xE7\u0131l\u0131r. Hi\xE7bir \u015Fey kendili\u011Finden g\xF6nderilmez.",
        "You started.": "Ba\u015Flad\u0131n.",
        "Just two minutes": "Sadece iki dakika",
        "That was the hardest part. Stop here with a clear conscience, or keep going while you\u2019re warm.": "En zor k\u0131s\u0131m buydu. \u0130\xE7in rahat, burada durabilirsin. Ya da \u0131s\u0131nm\u0131\u015Fken devam et.",
        "You don\u2019t have to finish. Just start \u201C{title}\u201D. When the time is up, you may stop.": "Bitirmek zorunda de\u011Filsin. Sadece ba\u015Fla: \u201C{title}\u201D. S\xFCre dolunca durabilirsin.",
        "{time} left": "{time} kald\u0131",
        "Two minutes are up.": "\u0130ki dakika doldu.",
        "I did it \u2014 mark as done": "Yapt\u0131m, i\u015Faretle",
        "Keep going with a focus timer": "Odak sayac\u0131yla devam et",
        "Stop for now": "\u015Eimdilik dur",
        "Today I decided: \u201C{title}\u201D. Ask me tonight if I did it.": "Bug\xFCn \u015Funa karar verdim: \u201C{title}\u201D. Ak\u015Fam bana yap\u0131p yapmad\u0131\u011F\u0131m\u0131 sor.",
        "Evidence": "Kan\u0131tlar",
        "Proof that you keep your word": "S\xF6z\xFCn\xFC tuttu\u011Funun kan\u0131t\u0131",
        "Once already, you did what you said you would. That is who you are becoming.": "S\xF6yledi\u011Fini \u015Fimdiden bir kez yapt\u0131n. D\xF6n\xFC\u015Ft\xFC\u011F\xFCn ki\u015Fi bu.",
        "{n} times you did what you said you would. That is who you are becoming.": "{n} kez s\xF6yledi\u011Fini yapt\u0131n. D\xF6n\xFC\u015Ft\xFC\u011F\xFCn ki\u015Fi bu.",
        "Every decision you keep will be written here. Motivation often follows action, and this list is how you\u2019ll see it.": "Tuttu\u011Fun her karar buraya yaz\u0131lacak. Motivasyon \xE7o\u011Fu zaman eylemden sonra gelir; bunu bu listede g\xF6receksin.",
        "Kept decisions": "Tutulan kararlar",
        "Days with a kept decision": "Karar\u0131n\u0131 tuttu\u011Fun g\xFCnler",
        "Go to today\u2019s decision": "Bug\xFCn\xFCn karar\u0131na git",
        "with a plan": "planl\u0131",
        "started with 2 minutes": "2 dakikayla ba\u015Flad\u0131n",
        "Your evidence": "Kan\u0131tlar\u0131n",
        "Every decision you kept": "Tuttu\u011Fun her karar",
        "Copied. Send it to one person you trust.": "Kopyaland\u0131. G\xFCvendi\u011Fin bir ki\u015Fiye g\xF6nder.",
        "Sharing isn\u2019t available here.": "Payla\u015F\u0131m burada kullan\u0131lam\u0131yor.",
        "If {obstacle}": "\u015Eu olursa: {obstacle}",
        "If it gets hard": "Zorla\u015F\u0131rsa",
        "then I will {plan}": "o zaman: {plan}",
        "That\u2019s proof #{n} that you keep your word.": "Bu, s\xF6z\xFCn\xFC tuttu\u011Funun {n}. kan\u0131t\u0131.",
        "Start \xB7 just 2 minutes": "Ba\u015Fla \xB7 sadece 2 dakika",
        "Plan for obstacles \xB7 30 sec": "Engellere plan yap \xB7 30 sn",
        "Tell one person": "Birine anlat",
        "Too big": "\xC7ok b\xFCy\xFCk",
        "Make it smaller. What is the first piece you could finish in two minutes?": "K\xFC\xE7\xFClt. \u0130ki dakikada bitirebilece\u011Fin ilk par\xE7a ne?",
        "Boring": "S\u0131k\u0131c\u0131",
        "Boring is allowed. Pair it with something you enjoy, or promise yourself only two minutes.": "S\u0131k\u0131c\u0131 olmas\u0131 serbest. Sevdi\u011Fin bir \u015Feyle e\u015Fle\u015Ftir ya da kendine sadece iki dakika s\xF6z ver.",
        "Scary": "Korkutucu",
        "Fear often means it matters. You don\u2019t need to feel ready to take one small step.": "Korku \xE7o\u011Fu zaman \xF6nemli oldu\u011Funu g\xF6sterir. K\xFC\xE7\xFCk bir ad\u0131m atmak i\xE7in haz\u0131r hissetmen gerekmez.",
        "Unclear": "Belirsiz",
        "Unclear tasks stall. Write down the very first physical action, like opening the file.": "Belirsiz i\u015Fler tak\u0131l\u0131r. \u0130lk fiziksel hareketi yaz; \xF6rne\u011Fin dosyay\u0131 a\xE7mak.",
        "I\u2019m okay": "\u0130yiyim",
        "Good. Protect this moment and start before the feeling changes.": "G\xFCzel. Bu an\u0131 koru ve his de\u011Fi\u015Fmeden ba\u015Fla.",
        "Yes": "Evet",
        "Your practice": "Prati\u011Fin",
        "Reminders, language, backup, appearance": "Hat\u0131rlatmalar, dil, yedekleme, g\xF6r\xFCn\xFCm",
        "More tools": "Di\u011Fer ara\xE7lar",
        "Your decision is still open: \u201C{title}\u201D. Two minutes is enough to start.": "Karar\u0131n h\xE2l\xE2 a\xE7\u0131k: \u201C{title}\u201D. Ba\u015Flamak i\xE7in iki dakika yeter.",
        "You haven\u2019t chosen today\u2019s decision yet. What one small thing would make today count?": "Bug\xFCn\xFCn karar\u0131n\u0131 hen\xFCz se\xE7medin. Bug\xFCn\xFC de\u011Ferli k\u0131lacak k\xFC\xE7\xFCk bir \u015Fey ne olabilir?",
        "Saved. Your one change will be here all week.": "Kaydedildi. Tek de\u011Fi\u015Fikli\u011Fin bu hafta boyunca burada olacak.",
        "Weekly look-back \xB7 2 minutes": "Haftal\u0131k geriye bak\u0131\u015F \xB7 2 dakika",
        "This week you kept your word on 1 day.": "Bu hafta 1 g\xFCn s\xF6z\xFCn\xFC tuttun.",
        "This week you kept your word on {n} days.": "Bu hafta {n} g\xFCn s\xF6z\xFCn\xFC tuttun.",
        "No grades. Just notice what worked, so next week is a little easier.": "Kimse not vermiyor. Sadece neyin i\u015Fe yarad\u0131\u011F\u0131n\u0131 fark et; gelecek hafta biraz daha kolay olsun.",
        "What helped this week?": "Bu hafta ne i\u015Fine yarad\u0131?",
        "e.g. deciding the night before": "\xF6rn. bir \xF6nceki gece karar vermek",
        "What got in the way?": "Ne engel oldu?",
        "e.g. starting too late in the day": "\xF6rn. g\xFCne \xE7ok ge\xE7 ba\u015Flamak",
        "One thing to change next week": "Gelecek hafta de\u011Fi\u015Ftirece\u011Fin bir \u015Fey",
        "e.g. do the decision before checking messages": "\xF6rn. karar\u0131m\u0131 mesajlara bakmadan \xF6nce yapmak",
        "Save my look-back": "Geriye bak\u0131\u015F\u0131m\u0131 kaydet",
        "Later": "Daha sonra",
        "This week\u2019s one change": "Bu haftan\u0131n tek de\u011Fi\u015Fikli\u011Fi",
        "Who you want to become first, then the places and things you\u2019d love. Choose one and give it a first step.": "\xD6nce kim olmak istedi\u011Fin, sonra gitmek istedi\u011Fin yerler ve sahip olmak istedi\u011Fin \u015Feyler. Birini se\xE7 ve ona bir ilk ad\u0131m ver.",
        "Skills & learning": "Beceriler ve \xF6\u011Frenme",
        "Things you can learn, finish and make with your own hands.": "Kendi ellerinle \xF6\u011Frenip bitirebilece\u011Fin ve yapabilece\u011Fin \u015Feyler.",
        "Health & energy": "Sa\u011Fl\u0131k ve enerji",
        "A stronger body, a calmer mind and more energy for everything else.": "Daha g\xFC\xE7l\xFC bir beden, daha sakin bir zihin ve her \u015Fey i\xE7in daha fazla enerji.",
        "Family & friends": "Aile ve arkada\u015Flar",
        "Time with the people who matter, planned instead of postponed.": "Ertelemek yerine planlanm\u0131\u015F, \xF6nemli insanlarla ge\xE7en zaman.",
        "Giving back": "Kar\u015F\u0131l\u0131k beklemeden vermek",
        "Ways your effort can change someone else\u2019s life too.": "Eme\u011Finin ba\u015Fka birinin hayat\u0131n\u0131 da de\u011Fi\u015Ftirebilece\u011Fi yollar.",
        "Work & money": "\u0130\u015F ve para",
        "Your own business, no debt and room to make brave choices.": "Kendi i\u015Fin, bor\xE7suz bir hayat ve cesur se\xE7imler yapabilecek alan.",
        "Journeys of the heart, slow weeks in beautiful cities, safaris and alpine retreats.": "Kalbin yolculuklar\u0131, g\xFCzel \u015Fehirlerde yava\u015F ge\xE7en haftalar, safariler ve da\u011F inzivalar\u0131.",
        "Play a piece you love on the piano": "Piyanoda sevdi\u011Fin bir par\xE7ay\u0131 \xE7al",
        "A year of weekly lessons and daily 15-minute practice, until one song you love lives in your hands.": "Bir y\u0131l boyunca haftal\u0131k dersler ve her g\xFCn 15 dakikal\u0131k pratik; ta ki sevdi\u011Fin bir \u015Fark\u0131 ellerinde ya\u015Fayana kadar.",
        "Proof that you can still learn something hard, slowly and joyfully.": "Zor bir \u015Feyi h\xE2l\xE2, yava\u015F yava\u015F ve keyifle \xF6\u011Frenebildi\u011Finin kan\u0131t\u0131.",
        "Book one trial lesson this week and choose the song.": "Bu hafta bir deneme dersi ay\u0131rt ve \u015Fark\u0131n\u0131 se\xE7.",
        "15 minutes a day": "G\xFCnde 15 dakika",
        "One song, then more": "\xD6nce bir \u015Fark\u0131, sonra daha fazlas\u0131",
        "Weekly teacher": "Haftal\u0131k \xF6\u011Fretmen",
        "Hold a real conversation in a new language": "Yeni bir dilde ger\xE7ek bir sohbet y\xFCr\xFCt",
        "Six months of daily practice and weekly conversation sessions, ending with a 30-minute talk with a native speaker.": "Alt\u0131 ay boyunca her g\xFCn pratik ve haftal\u0131k konu\u015Fma seanslar\u0131, sonunda anadili konu\u015Fan biriyle 30 dakikal\u0131k bir sohbet.",
        "A new language opens people, places and a new version of you.": "Yeni bir dil; insanlar\u0131, yerleri ve yeni bir seni a\xE7ar.",
        "Pick the language and do ten minutes of practice today.": "Dili se\xE7 ve bug\xFCn on dakika pratik yap.",
        "Daily 10 minutes": "G\xFCnl\xFCk 10 dakika",
        "Weekly speaking": "Haftal\u0131k konu\u015Fma",
        "Six months": "Alt\u0131 ay",
        "Build and ship your first app": "\u0130lk uygulaman\u0131 geli\u015Ftir ve yay\u0131nla",
        "Learn the basics of programming and publish one small tool that real people use.": "Programlaman\u0131n temellerini \xF6\u011Fren ve ger\xE7ek insanlar\u0131n kulland\u0131\u011F\u0131 k\xFC\xE7\xFCk bir ara\xE7 yay\u0131nla.",
        "Turning ideas into working things is a skill that compounds for life.": "Fikirleri \xE7al\u0131\u015Fan \u015Feylere d\xF6n\xFC\u015Ft\xFCrmek, \xF6m\xFCr boyu katlanarak b\xFCy\xFCyen bir beceri.",
        "Finish the first lesson of a free beginner course tonight.": "Bu ak\u015Fam \xFCcretsiz bir ba\u015Flang\u0131\xE7 kursunun ilk dersini bitir.",
