      "2:250",
      "Bakara",
      "C\xE2l\xFBt ve ordusuyla kar\u015F\u0131 kar\u015F\u0131ya geldiklerinde \u015F\xF6yle dediler: Rabbimiz, \xFCzerimize bolca sab\u0131r d\xF6k, ayaklar\u0131m\u0131z\u0131 sa\u011Flam tut ve ink\xE2r eden bu toplulu\u011Fa kar\u015F\u0131 bize yard\u0131m et.",
      "When they faced Goliath and his forces, they said: Our Lord, pour patience upon us, keep our feet firm, and help us against the people who deny You.",
      ["courage", "patience", "prayer"]
    ),
    q2(
      "adaptation",
      "2:260",
      "Bakara",
      "\u0130brahim, inand\u0131\u011F\u0131 h\xE2lde kalbinin yat\u0131\u015Fmas\u0131n\u0131 istedi. \u0130\xE7indeki soruyu saklamak zorunda de\u011Filsin; anlamaya \xE7al\u0131\u015Fmak ve g\xFCven aramak, inanc\u0131nla birlikte y\xFCr\xFCyebilece\u011Fin samimi bir ara\u015Ft\u0131rma olabilir.",
      "Abraham believed and still asked for his heart to settle. You need not hide your questions; seeking understanding and reassurance can be an honest inquiry alongside faith.",
      ["uncertainty", "faith", "learning"]
    ),
    q2(
      "translation",
      "3:8",
      "\xC2l-i \u0130mr\xE2n",
      "Rabbimiz, bize yolu g\xF6sterdikten sonra kalplerimizi o yoldan sapt\u0131rma; bize kendi kat\u0131ndan bir rahmet ba\u011F\u0131\u015Fla. \u015E\xFCphesiz, kar\u015F\u0131l\u0131k beklemeden bol bol ba\u011F\u0131\u015Fta bulunan sensin.",
      "Our Lord, do not let our hearts turn aside after You have guided us. Give us mercy from Your presence; You are the One who freely and abundantly gives.",
      ["uncertainty", "prayer", "steadiness"]
    ),
    q2(
      "translation",
      "3:103",
      "\xC2l-i \u0130mr\xE2n",
      "Hep birlikte Allah\u2019\u0131n ipine tutunun, ayr\u0131l\u0131\u011Fa d\xFC\u015Fmeyin. \xDCzerinizdeki nimetini hat\u0131rlay\u0131n: Birbirinize d\xFC\u015Fmanken kalplerinizi birbirine \u0131s\u0131nd\u0131rd\u0131; b\xF6ylece O\u2019nun nimeti sayesinde siz birbirinizin karde\u015Fi oldunuz.",
      "Together, hold firmly to God\u2019s rope and do not split apart. Remember His gift to you: He brought your hearts together when you were enemies, making you brothers through His grace.",
      ["connection", "gratitude", "reconciliation"],
      true,
      "https://quran.com/ali-imran/103"
    ),
    q2(
      "translation",
      "3:190-191",
      "\xC2l-i \u0130mr\xE2n",
      "Onlar ayaktayken, otururken ve yanlar\u0131 \xFCzerine uzanm\u0131\u015Fken Allah\u2019\u0131 anar; g\xF6klerin ve yerin yarat\u0131l\u0131\u015F\u0131 \xFCzerine d\xFC\u015F\xFCn\xFCrler: Rabbimiz, bunu bo\u015Funa yaratmad\u0131n. Seni eksiklikten uzak tutar\u0131z; bizi ate\u015Fin azab\u0131ndan koru.",
      "They remember God while standing, sitting, and resting on their sides, reflecting on the making of heaven and earth: Our Lord, You made none of this without purpose. Glory to You; protect us from the fire.",
      ["reflection", "meaning", "prayer"],
      true
