    q2(
      "translation",
      "7:23",
      "A\u2018r\xE2f",
      "\u0130kisi \u015F\xF6yle dedi: Rabbimiz, biz kendimize haks\u0131zl\u0131k ettik. E\u011Fer bizi ba\u011F\u0131\u015Flamaz ve bize merhamet etmezsen, hi\xE7 \u015F\xFCphe yok ki kayba u\u011Frayan kimselerden olaca\u011F\u0131z.",
      "The two said: Our Lord, we have wronged ourselves. Unless You forgive us and show us mercy, we will certainly be among those who have lost.",
      ["repentance", "honesty", "hope"]
    ),
    q2(
      "adaptation",
      "7:55",
      "A\u2018r\xE2f",
      "Duan\u0131 duyurmak i\xE7in sesini b\xFCy\xFCtmen gerekmiyor. \u0130\xE7tenlikle ve sakince Rabbine y\xF6nel; ba\u015Fkalar\u0131n\u0131n g\xF6rmedi\u011Fi bir niyaz da kalbinin en d\xFCr\xFCst yerinden y\xFCkselebilir, g\xF6steri\u015Fe ihtiya\xE7 duymaz.",
      "Your prayer need not grow louder to be heard. Turn to your Lord quietly and sincerely; a plea unseen by others can rise from your heart\u2019s most honest place without display.",
      ["prayer", "sincerity", "calm"],
      false,
      "https://quran.com/al-araf/55"
    ),
    q2(
      "translation",
      "8:24",
      "Enf\xE2l",
      "Ey iman edenler, size hayat verecek olana \xE7a\u011F\u0131rd\u0131\u011F\u0131nda Allah\u2019a ve El\xE7i\u2019ye kar\u015F\u0131l\u0131k verin. Bilin ki Allah, insanla kalbinin aras\u0131na girer; sonunda O\u2019nun huzurunda toplanacaks\u0131n\u0131z.",
      "Believers, answer God and the Messenger when he calls you toward what gives you life. Know that God comes between a person and the heart, and that you will be gathered to Him.",
      ["courage", "response", "life"]
    ),
    q2(
      "translation",
      "8:46",
      "Enf\xE2l",
      "Allah\u2019a ve El\xE7isi\u2019ne itaat edin; birbirinizle \xE7eki\u015Fmeyin, yoksa cesaretiniz k\u0131r\u0131l\u0131r ve g\xFCc\xFCn\xFCz da\u011F\u0131l\u0131r. Sab\u0131rla direnmeye devam edin; hi\xE7 \u015F\xFCphesiz Allah, sabreden kimselerle beraberdir.",
      "Obey God and His Messenger, and do not quarrel with one another, weakening your courage and scattering your strength. Remain patient; God is with those who endure.",
      ["courage", "cooperation", "patience"]
    ),
    q2(
      "translation",
      "10:57",
      "Y\xFBnus",
      "Ey insanlar, size Rabbinizden bir \xF6\u011F\xFCt geldi; g\xF6n\xFCllerde olana bir \u015Fifa, iman edenler i\xE7in de do\u011Fru yolu g\xF6steren bir rehber ve bir rahmet.",
      "People, a counsel has reached you from your Lord: a healing for what hearts contain, and guidance and mercy for those who believe.",
      ["hope", "heart", "guidance"]
    ),
    q2(
      "adaptation",
      "10:58",
      "Y\xFBnus",
      "Sevinmek i\xE7in yaln\u0131zca biriktirdiklerine bakma. Allah\u2019\u0131n l\xFCtfunu ve merhametini fark etti\u011Fin bir an da k\u0131ymetlidir; bug\xFCn\xFCn sevincini sahip olduklar\u0131n\u0131n say\u0131s\u0131na hapsetmeden ya\u015Famay\u0131 deneyebilirsin.",
      "Do not look only at what you have accumulated when seeking joy. A moment of noticing God\u2019s grace and mercy matters too; let today\u2019s happiness reach beyond your possessions.",
      ["hope", "gratitude", "joy"]
    ),
    q2(
      "adaptation",
      "11:61",
      "H\xFBd",
      "S\xE2lih\u2019in \xE7a\u011Fr\u0131s\u0131, insan\u0131n yery\xFCz\xFCndeki yerini emek ve imarla ili\u015Fkilendirir. Bulundu\u011Fun yeri biraz daha ya\u015Fan\u0131r k\u0131l: onard\u0131\u011F\u0131n, yeti\u015Ftirdi\u011Fin veya korudu\u011Fun \u015Feyle sorumlulu\u011Funu bug\xFCn g\xF6r\xFCn\xFCr h\xE2le getir.",
      "Salih\u2019s call connects our place on earth with cultivating it. Make your surroundings more livable: let what you repair, grow, or protect give your responsibility visible form today.",
      ["work", "stewardship", "action"]
    ),
    q2(
      "adaptation",
      "12:47-49",
      "Y\xFBsuf",
      "Y\xFBsuf, zor y\u0131llar\u0131 d\xFC\u015F\xFCn\xFCrken insanlar\u0131 korkuda b\u0131rakmad\u0131; ekmeyi, saklamay\u0131 ve \xF6l\xE7\xFCl\xFC kullanmay\u0131 anlatt\u0131. Belirsizli\u011Fin kar\u015F\u0131s\u0131na bug\xFCn uygulanabilir bir haz\u0131rl\u0131k koy; kayg\u0131n\u0131 k\xFC\xE7\xFCk bir plana \xE7evirebilirsin.",
      "Joseph did not leave people stranded in fear of difficult years; he described planting, storing, and using resources carefully. Meet uncertainty with practical preparation: give anxiety a small, workable plan.",
      ["uncertainty", "preparation", "action"]
    ),
    q2(
      "adaptation",
      "12:67",
      "Y\xFBsuf",
      "Ya\u2018k\u016Bb, \xE7ocuklar\u0131na ayr\u0131 kap\u0131lardan girmelerini s\xF6ylerken Allah\u2019a g\xFCvendi\u011Fini de belirtti. Elindeki tedbiri almak g\xFCvenini azaltmaz; haz\u0131rl\u0131\u011F\u0131n\u0131 yapabilir, her sonucu tek ba\u015F\u0131na y\xF6netme y\xFCk\xFCn\xFC b\u0131rakabilirsin.",
      "Jacob advised his children to enter through different gates while affirming trust in God. Precaution need not weaken trust: prepare responsibly and release the burden of controlling every outcome.",
      ["uncertainty", "trust", "preparation"]
    ),
    q2(
      "adaptation",
      "12:87",
      "Y\xFBsuf",
      "Ya\u2018k\u016Bb\u2019un \xFCmidi, \xE7ocuklar\u0131n\u0131 Y\xFBsuf\u2019u ve karde\u015Fini aramaya g\xF6nderdi. Umut bazen yerinde beklemekten fazlas\u0131n\u0131 ister; hen\xFCz her \u015Feyi bilmesen de ara\u015Ft\u0131rabilir, sorabilir, bir kap\u0131y\u0131 \xE7alabilirsin.",
      "Jacob\u2019s hope sent his children searching for Joseph and his brother. Hope sometimes asks more than waiting; without knowing everything yet, you can investigate, ask, and knock on a door.",
      ["hope", "courage", "action"]
    ),
    q2(
      "adaptation",
      "13:17",
      "Ra\u2018d",
      "Suyun y\xFCz\xFCndeki k\xF6p\xFCk dikkat \xE7eker, fakat insanlara yarayan kal\u0131r. G\xFCr\xFClt\xFCl\xFC sonu\xE7lar seni aceleye s\xFCr\xFCkledi\u011Finde yapt\u0131\u011F\u0131n i\u015Fin ger\xE7ek faydas\u0131n\u0131 sor; sessizce i\u015Fe yarayan\u0131 k\xFC\xE7\xFCmsememeyi \xF6\u011Fren.",
      "Foam draws attention on the water, yet what benefits people remains. When noisy results make you rush, ask what your work truly contributes; learn to value what quietly serves.",
      ["uncertainty", "purpose", "patience"]
    ),
    q2(
      "translation",
      "16:78",
      "Nahl",
      "Allah sizi annelerinizin kar\u0131nlar\u0131ndan hi\xE7bir \u015Fey bilmezken \xE7\u0131kard\u0131. \u015E\xFCkretmeniz i\xE7in de size i\u015Fitme duyusu, g\xF6rme yetisi ve d\xFC\u015F\xFCn\xFCp anlayaca\u011F\u0131n\u0131z g\xF6n\xFCller verdi.",
      "God brought you from your mothers\u2019 wombs knowing nothing, and gave you hearing, sight, and hearts, so that you might be thankful.",
      ["gratitude", "learning", "attention"]
    ),
    q2(
      "translation",
      "17:70",
      "\u0130sr\xE2",
      "Andolsun, \xC2demo\u011Fullar\u0131na de\u011Fer ve onur verdik; onlar\u0131 karada ve denizde ta\u015F\u0131d\u0131k, temiz ve g\xFCzel \u015Feylerle besledik ve yaratt\u0131klar\u0131m\u0131z\u0131n bir\xE7o\u011Funa g\xF6re onlara belirgin bir \xFCst\xFCnl\xFCk verdik.",
      "We have honored Adam\u2019s children, carried them over land and sea, provided wholesome things for them, and favored them greatly above many of Our creatures.",
      ["dignity", "gratitude", "humanity"]
    ),
    q2(
      "translation",
      "18:10",
      "Kehf",
      "O gen\xE7ler ma\u011Faraya s\u0131\u011F\u0131nm\u0131\u015F ve \u015F\xF6yle demi\u015Flerdi: Rabbimiz, bize kendi kat\u0131ndan bir rahmet ver; i\xE7inde bulundu\u011Fumuz bu i\u015Fte bize do\u011Fru bir \xE7\u0131k\u0131\u015F yolu haz\u0131rla.",
      "The young people took refuge in the cave and said: Our Lord, grant us mercy from Your presence and prepare a sound way forward through our situation.",
      ["courage", "uncertainty", "prayer"]
    ),
    q2(
      "adaptation",
      "18:14",
      "Kehf",
      "Ma\u011Fara arkada\u015Flar\u0131n\u0131n kalpleri, inan\xE7lar\u0131n\u0131 dile getirmek \xFCzere aya\u011Fa kalkt\u0131klar\u0131nda g\xFC\xE7lendirildi. Cesareti yaln\u0131zca i\xE7inden ge\xE7en bir his sanma; do\u011Fru buldu\u011Fun s\xF6z\xFC sayg\u0131yla s\xF6ylemek de onu besleyebilir.",
      "The companions of the cave were strengthened in heart when they stood to declare their belief. Courage is more than an inward feeling; respectfully speaking what you hold true can nourish it.",
      ["courage", "faith", "action"],
      false,
      "https://quran.com/al-kahf/14"
    ),
    q2(
      "adaptation",
      "18:95",
      "Kehf",
      "Z\xFClkarneyn, bir engeli a\u015Fmak isteyen insanlardan emekleriyle yard\u0131m istedi. Ortak bir sorunun \xF6n\xFCnde yaln\u0131z kahraman arama; becerini ortaya koy, birlikte kurulacak \xE7\xF6z\xFCmde kendi pay\u0131n\u0131 \xFCstlen.",
      "Dhul-Qarnayn asked people to contribute their strength toward a protective barrier. A shared problem need not await one hero; offer your skill and take your part in building a solution together.",
      ["cooperation", "work", "responsibility"]
    ),
    q2(
      "adaptation",
      "19:4",
      "Meryem",
      "Zekeriyy\xE2 duas\u0131nda ya\u015F\u0131n\u0131 ve g\xFC\xE7s\xFCzl\xFC\u011F\xFCn\xFC saklamad\u0131; Rabbine \xFCmidini de s\xF6yledi. G\xFC\xE7l\xFC g\xF6r\xFCnmek u\u011Fruna yorgunlu\u011Funu gizleme; ihtiyac\u0131n\u0131 d\xFCr\xFCst\xE7e dile getirmen, g\xFCvenle yeniden y\xF6nelmenin bir yolu olabilir.",
      "Zechariah\u2019s prayer concealed neither age nor weakness, yet still voiced hope in his Lord. You need not hide exhaustion to appear strong; naming your need honestly can be a way of returning with trust.",
      ["hope", "vulnerability", "prayer"]
    ),
    q2(
      "translation",
      "20:45-46",
      "T\xE2h\xE2",
      "\u0130kisi, Rabbimiz, onun bize sald\u0131rmas\u0131ndan veya iyice azg\u0131nla\u015Fmas\u0131ndan korkuyoruz, dediler. Allah \u015F\xF6yle dedi: Korkmay\u0131n; ben sizinle beraberim, s\xF6ylenenleri i\u015Fitiyor, olup bitenleri g\xF6r\xFCyorum.",
      "They said: Our Lord, we fear that he may attack us or exceed all bounds. He said: Do not fear; I am with you both, hearing and seeing.",
      ["fear", "courage", "trust"],
      false,
      "https://quran.com/taha/45-46"
    ),
    q2(
      "adaptation",
      "20:67-69",
      "T\xE2h\xE2",
      "M\xFBs\xE2\u2019n\u0131n i\xE7ine korku d\xFC\u015Ft\xFC; ard\u0131ndan elindekini ortaya koymas\u0131 istendi. Korkunun varl\u0131\u011F\u0131 ad\u0131m\u0131n\u0131 imk\xE2ns\u0131z k\u0131lmaz. Haz\u0131rlad\u0131\u011F\u0131n \u015Feyi kullan, yapabilece\u011Fin i\u015Fi se\xE7 ve titreyen kalbinle de ba\u015Flayabilece\u011Fini hat\u0131rla.",
      "Moses felt fear within and was then told to cast what he held. Fear does not make action impossible: use what you have prepared and remember that a trembling heart can still begin.",
      ["fear", "courage", "action"],
      false,
      "https://quran.com/taha/67-69"
    ),
    q2(
      "adaptation",
      "21:89",
      "Enbiy\xE2",
      "Zekeriyy\xE2, evlat \xF6zlemini Rabbine a\xE7arken yaln\u0131zl\u0131\u011F\u0131n\u0131 da dile getirdi. \u0130\xE7inde uzun s\xFCredir ta\u015F\u0131d\u0131\u011F\u0131n bir iste\u011Fi k\xFC\xE7\xFCmseme; onu a\xE7\u0131k\xE7a s\xF6ylemek, \xFCmidine d\xFCr\xFCst bir yer a\xE7abilir.",
      "Zechariah voiced loneliness as he brought his longing for a child to his Lord. Do not belittle a hope you have carried for years; naming it can make an honest place for hope.",
      ["hope", "longing", "prayer"]
    ),
    q2(
      "adaptation",
      "26:61-63",
      "\u015Euar\xE2",
      "Denizin \xF6n\xFCnde M\xFBs\xE2\u2019n\u0131n arkada\u015Flar\u0131 yakalanacaklar\u0131n\u0131 d\xFC\u015F\xFCnd\xFC; M\xFBs\xE2 rehberlik umudunu korudu ve kendisine bildirilen hareketi yapt\u0131. \xD6n\xFCn kapal\u0131 g\xF6r\xFCn\xFCrken b\xFCt\xFCn ihtimalleri bitmi\u015F saymadan bir y\xF6n arayabilirsin.",
      "At the sea, Moses\u2019 companions thought they would be caught; he kept hope of guidance and made the instructed move. When the way appears closed, you can seek direction before declaring every possibility exhausted.",
      ["fear", "courage", "hope"],
      false,
      "https://quran.com/ash-shuara/62"
    ),
    q2(
      "adaptation",
      "28:7",
      "Kasas",
      "M\xFBs\xE2\u2019n\u0131n annesinin hik\xE2yesinde korku, koruma iste\u011Fiyle yan yanad\u0131r. Sevdiklerin i\xE7in kayg\u0131 duyarken kendine y\xFCklenme; elindeki sorumlulu\u011Fu dikkatle yerine getirip ta\u015F\u0131yamad\u0131\u011F\u0131n k\u0131sm\u0131 Allah\u2019a emanet edebilirsin.",
      "In the story of Moses\u2019 mother, fear stands beside the wish to protect. Do not condemn yourself for worrying about loved ones; fulfill your responsibility carefully and entrust what exceeds you to God.",
      ["fear", "care", "trust"],
      false,
      "https://quran.com/al-qasas/7"
    ),
    q2(
      "adaptation",
      "28:21",
      "Kasas",
      "M\xFBs\xE2 \u015Fehirden korkarak ve \xE7evresini g\xF6zeterek \xE7\u0131kt\u0131, kurtulu\u015F i\xE7in dua etti. Tehlikeden uzakla\u015Fmak cesaret eksikli\u011Fi de\u011Fildir; dikkatli bir \xE7\u0131k\u0131\u015F ararken Allah\u2019tan yard\u0131m istemek de m\xFCmk\xFCnd\xFCr.",
      "Moses left the city afraid and watchful, praying for deliverance. Moving away from danger need not mean a lack of courage; seeking a careful exit and asking God for help can belong together.",
      ["fear", "courage", "prudence"]
    ),
    q2(
      "adaptation",
      "28:22",
      "Kasas",
      "M\xFBs\xE2 Medyen\u2019e y\xF6nelirken yolunun b\xFCt\xFCn ayr\u0131nt\u0131lar\u0131n\u0131 bilmiyordu; Rabbinden do\u011Fru yola iletilmeyi umuyordu. Her cevap elinde olmadan da makul bir y\xF6ne d\xF6nebilir, y\xFCr\xFCrken \xF6\u011Frenmeye a\xE7\u0131k kalabilirsin.",
      "Heading toward Midian, Moses hoped his Lord would guide him along a sound way. You can turn toward a reasonable direction before every answer is available and remain ready to learn while moving.",
      ["uncertainty", "courage", "action"]
    ),
    q2(
      "adaptation",
      "28:34",
      "Kasas",
      "M\xFBs\xE2, karde\u015Fi H\xE2r\xFBn\u2019un daha a\xE7\u0131k konu\u015Ftu\u011Funu s\xF6yledi ve deste\u011Fini istedi. Zor bir konu\u015Fmadan korkuyorsan her \u015Feyi tek ba\u015F\u0131na ta\u015F\u0131mak zorunda de\u011Filsin; uygun bir yard\u0131mc\u0131 istemek haz\u0131rl\u0131\u011F\u0131n par\xE7as\u0131d\u0131r.",
      "Moses named Aaron\u2019s clearer speech and asked for his support. If a difficult conversation frightens you, you need not carry it alone; requesting suitable help is part of preparation.",
      ["fear", "courage", "support"]
    ),
    q2(
      "translation",
      "39:18",
      "Z\xFCmer",
      "Onlar s\xF6z\xFC dinler ve onun en g\xFCzeline uyarlar. \u0130\u015Fte bunlar, Allah\u2019\u0131n do\u011Fru yola iletti\u011Fi kimselerdir; d\xFC\u015F\xFCn\xFCp anlayan ak\u0131l sahipleri de i\u015Fte bu kimselerdir.",
      "They listen to what is said and follow the best of it. These are the ones God has guided; these are the people of discerning minds.",
      ["listening", "discernment", "learning"]
    ),
    q2(
      "translation",
      "42:38",
      "\u015E\xFBr\xE2",
      "Onlar Rablerinin \xE7a\u011Fr\u0131s\u0131na kar\u015F\u0131l\u0131k verir, namaz\u0131 dosdo\u011Fru k\u0131larlar. \u0130\u015Flerini kendi aralar\u0131nda dan\u0131\u015Farak y\xFCr\xFCt\xFCr ve kendilerine r\u0131z\u0131k olarak verdiklerimizden ba\u015Fkalar\u0131 i\xE7in de harcamada bulunurlar.",
      "They answer their Lord, keep up prayer, conduct their affairs through mutual consultation, and give to others from the provision We have granted them.",
      ["consultation", "generosity", "responsibility"]
    ),
    q2(
      "adaptation",
      "48:4",
      "Fetih",
      "\u0130man edenlerin kalplerine s\xFCk\xFBnet indirildi\u011Fi anlat\u0131l\u0131r. \u0130\xE7indeki tela\u015F\u0131n hep ayn\u0131 kalaca\u011F\u0131n\u0131 d\xFC\u015F\xFCnme; kalbin i\xE7in ferahl\u0131k isterken bug\xFCn \xF6n\xFCndeki i\u015Fi daha sakin ele almaya alan a\xE7abilirsin.",
      "The passage describes tranquility being sent into believing hearts. Inner turmoil need not feel permanent; as you ask for spaciousness within, make room to approach today\u2019s task more calmly.",
      ["hope", "calm", "faith"]
    ),
    c(
      "Abu Bakr",
      "Hz. Eb\xFB Bekir",
      "bukhari",
      "3667",
      "Eb\xFB Bekir, Peygamber\u2019in vefat\u0131ndaki b\xFCy\xFCk sars\u0131nt\u0131da insanlara Allah\u2019\u0131n diri oldu\u011Funu hat\u0131rlatt\u0131. Yas\u0131n ortas\u0131nda sevdi\u011Finin de\u011Ferini korurken, hayat\u0131n\u0131 ayakta tutacak inanca yeniden tutunabilece\u011Fin bir yer arayabilirsin.",
      "In the shock of the Prophet\u2019s death, Abu Bakr reminded people that God lives. Amid grief, you can honor the person you loved while seeking an anchor in the faith that sustains you.",
      ["grief", "hope", "steadiness"]
    ),
    c(
      "Abu Bakr",
      "Hz. Eb\xFB Bekir",
      "bukhari",
      "4750",
      "Eb\xFB Bekir, ailesini inciten iftiraya kat\u0131lm\u0131\u015F bir yak\u0131n\u0131na verdi\u011Fi yard\u0131m\u0131 yeniden ba\u015Flatt\u0131. K\u0131rg\u0131nl\u0131\u011F\u0131n ger\xE7ektir; yine de iyili\u011Fini yaln\u0131zca incinmi\u015Fli\u011Finin y\xF6netmesine izin vermeyecek bir yol d\xFC\u015F\xFCnebilirsin.",
      "Abu Bakr resumed supporting a relative who had joined a slander against his family. Your hurt is real; you can still consider a way for goodness not to be governed solely by that hurt.",
      ["forgiveness", "courage", "generosity"]
    ),
    c(
      "Abu Bakr",
      "Hz. Eb\xFB Bekir",
      "muslim",
      "1028b",
      "Eb\xFB Bekir ayn\u0131 g\xFCn oru\xE7 tutmu\u015F, cenazeye kat\u0131lm\u0131\u015F, bir yoksulu doyurmu\u015F ve hastay\u0131 ziyaret etmi\u015Fti. G\xFCn\xFCn i\xE7inde farkl\u0131 ihtiya\xE7lar\u0131 fark et; ibadetle insanlara dokunan eme\u011Fi bulu\u015Fturabilirsin.",
      "In one day Abu Bakr had fasted, attended a funeral, fed someone poor, and visited the sick. Notice different needs within your day; devotion and work that reaches people can meet.",
      ["service", "attention", "action"]
    ),
    c(
      "Umar ibn al-Khattab",
      "Hz. \xD6mer",
      "bukhari",
      "2737",
      "\xD6mer, de\u011Ferli arazisini nas\u0131l hayra kullanaca\u011F\u0131n\u0131 dan\u0131\u015Ft\u0131; arazinin korunup \xFCr\xFCn\xFCn\xFCn payla\u015F\u0131lmas\u0131yla bir vak\u0131f kurdu. Elindeki imk\xE2n\u0131 t\xFCketmeden de faydas\u0131n\u0131 \xE7o\u011Faltman\u0131n, ba\u015Fkalar\u0131na s\xFCrekli kap\u0131 a\xE7man\u0131n yollar\u0131n\u0131 d\xFC\u015F\xFCnebilirsin.",
      "Umar sought counsel on using treasured land for good and endowed it so its produce could be shared. Consider ways for a resource to keep benefiting others without exhausting its foundation.",
      ["generosity", "consultation", "stewardship"]
    ),
    c(
      "Umar ibn al-Khattab",
      "Hz. \xD6mer",
      "bukhari",
      "89",
      "\xD6mer ve kom\u015Fusu \xF6\u011Frenmeye s\u0131rayla gidiyor, duyduklar\u0131n\u0131 birbirleriyle payla\u015F\u0131yordu. Her yere yeti\u015Femedi\u011Fin i\xE7in bilgiden vazge\xE7me; g\xFCvendi\u011Fin biriyle i\u015F b\xF6l\xFCm\xFC yaparak \xF6\u011Frenmeye hayat\u0131nda d\xFCzenli bir yer a\xE7abilirsin.",
      "Umar and his neighbor took turns attending lessons and shared what they heard. Being unable to be everywhere need not end learning; cooperate with someone trustworthy to give it a regular place in life.",
      ["learning", "cooperation", "action"]
    ),
    c(
      "Umar ibn al-Khattab",
      "Hz. \xD6mer",
      "bukhari",
      "1597",
      "\xD6mer, Hacer\xFClesved\u2019in kendi ba\u015F\u0131na zarar veya fayda veremeyece\u011Fini a\xE7\u0131k\xE7a s\xF6yledi. \u0130nanc\u0131n\u0131n dayana\u011F\u0131n\u0131 berrak tut; bir nesneye ta\u015F\u0131yamayaca\u011F\u0131 g\xFC\xE7ler y\xFCklemek yerine yapt\u0131\u011F\u0131n ibadetin anlam\u0131n\u0131 \xF6\u011Frenmeye y\xF6nel.",
      "Umar plainly stated that the Black Stone could neither harm nor benefit by itself. Keep faith\u2019s foundation clear; seek the meaning of your worship instead of assigning impossible powers to an object.",
      ["discernment", "faith", "clarity"]
    ),
    c(
      "Umar ibn al-Khattab",
      "Hz. \xD6mer",
      "bukhari",
      "4160",
      "\xD6mer, \xE7ocuklar\u0131 i\xE7in yard\u0131m isteyen kad\u0131n\u0131 dinledi; yiyecek, giyecek ve ba\u015Fka ihtiya\xE7lar\u0131yla destek oldu. Birinin s\u0131k\u0131nt\u0131s\u0131n\u0131 duydu\u011Funda ihtiyac\u0131n ad\u0131n\u0131 \xF6\u011Fren; ilgin somut bir kar\u015F\u0131l\u0131k bulabilsin.",
      "Umar listened to a woman asking for her children and provided food, clothing, and other necessities. When someone shares a hardship, learn what is needed so your attention can take practical form.",
      ["compassion", "listening", "service"]
    ),
    c(
      "Uthman ibn Affan",
      "Hz. Osman",
      "bukhari",
      "2778",
      "Osman, R\xFBme Kuyusu\u2019nun a\xE7\u0131lmas\u0131n\u0131 sa\u011Flad\u0131\u011F\u0131n\u0131 insanlara hat\u0131rlatt\u0131. Bir ihtiya\xE7 herkesin kar\u015F\u0131s\u0131na \xE7\u0131k\u0131yorsa \xE7\xF6z\xFCm\xFC yaln\u0131z kendine ay\u0131rma; elindeki imk\xE2n\u0131n \xF6l\xE7\xFCs\xFCnde ortak eri\u015Fimi kolayla\u015Ft\u0131rman\u0131n bir yolunu d\xFC\u015F\xFCn.",
      "Uthman reminded listeners that he had arranged for the well of Rumah to be dug. When a need confronts a whole community, consider how your resources might improve shared access rather than serve you alone.",
      ["generosity", "community", "action"]
    ),
    c(
      "Uthman ibn Affan",
      "Hz. Osman",
      "bukhari",
      "4987",
      "Osman, Kur\u2019an k\u0131raatindeki ayr\u0131l\u0131klar\u0131n b\xFCy\xFCmesi \xFCzerine n\xFCshalar\u0131n haz\u0131rlanmas\u0131n\u0131 bir heyete emanet etti. Ortak de\u011Ferleri korumak titizlik ister; farkl\u0131l\u0131k g\xF6rd\xFC\u011F\xFCnde bilgiyi denetle, ehil insanlarla birlikte \xE7\xF6z\xFCm \xFCret.",
      "When disputes over Quranic recitation grew, Uthman entrusted a committee with preparing copies. Protecting shared values calls for care: verify information and work with knowledgeable people toward a solution.",
      ["responsibility", "cooperation", "care"]
    ),
    c(
      "Ali ibn Abi Talib",
      "Hz. Ali",
      "bukhari",
      "111",
      "Ali, kendisinde ba\u015Fkalar\u0131ndan gizlenmi\u015F \xF6zel bir kitap bulundu\u011Fu iddias\u0131n\u0131 do\u011Frulamad\u0131; sahip oldu\u011Fu bilgiyi a\xE7\u0131k\xE7a anlatt\u0131. Bilmedi\u011Fine esrar katmak yerine bildi\u011Finin s\u0131n\u0131r\u0131n\u0131 d\xFCr\xFCst\xE7e s\xF6ylemek de g\xFCven verir.",
      "Ali did not endorse the claim that he possessed a special hidden book; he plainly described what he had. Trust can grow from honestly naming the limits of your knowledge instead of surrounding it with mystery.",
      ["honesty", "knowledge", "integrity"]
    ),
    c(
      "Bilal ibn Rabah",
      "Hz. Bil\xE2l",
      "bukhari",
      "1149",
      "Bil\xE2l, abdest ald\u0131\u011F\u0131nda imk\xE2n\u0131 \xF6l\xE7\xFCs\xFCnde namaz k\u0131lmay\u0131 en \xE7ok \xFCmit ba\u011Flad\u0131\u011F\u0131 ameli olarak anlatt\u0131. G\xFCn\xFCndeki bir haz\u0131rl\u0131\u011F\u0131 anlaml\u0131 bir davran\u0131\u015Fa ba\u011Fla; niyetine somut bir ba\u015Flang\u0131\xE7 noktas\u0131 kazand\u0131r.",
      "Bilal described praying as much as he could after ablution as the deed in which he placed greatest hope. Connect a daily preparation to meaningful action, giving your intention a concrete starting point.",
      ["hope", "devotion", "action"]
    ),
    c(
      "Salman al-Farisi",
      "Hz. Selm\xE2n-\u0131 F\xE2ris\xEE",
      "bukhari",
      "1968",
      "Selm\xE2n, dostunun evindeki ihmal edilmi\u015Fli\u011Fi fark etti ve onunla konu\u015Ftu. \u0130yi dostluk bazen sessizce onaylamakla yetinmez; sevdi\u011Finin fark etmedi\u011Fi y\xFCkleri incitmeden g\xF6r\xFCn\xFCr k\u0131lmak i\xE7in yan\u0131nda durur.",
      "Salman noticed neglect in his friend\u2019s household and spoke with him. Good friendship sometimes goes beyond quiet approval, staying close enough to gently reveal burdens a loved one has overlooked.",
      ["friendship", "courage", "care"]
    ),
    c(
      "Khadijah bint Khuwaylid",
      "Hz. Hatice",
      "bukhari",
      "3",
      "Hatice, korkuyla d\xF6nen Peygamber\u2019i teselli ederken onun insanlara yapt\u0131\u011F\u0131 iyilikleri tek tek hat\u0131rlatt\u0131. Kayg\u0131n b\xFCy\xFCd\xFC\u011F\xFCnde ge\xE7mi\u015Findeki ger\xE7ek dayan\u0131kl\u0131l\u0131k \xF6rneklerini an\u0131msa; g\xFCven bazen somut hat\u0131ralardan beslenir.",
      "Comforting the frightened Prophet, Khadijah named the good he had done for people. When anxiety grows, recall real examples of steadiness in your own history; confidence can be nourished by concrete memories.",
      ["fear", "courage", "support"]
    ),
    c(
      "Aishah bint Abi Bakr",
      "Hz. \xC2i\u015Fe",
      "bukhari",
      "103",
      "\xC2i\u015Fe, anlamad\u0131\u011F\u0131 bir s\xF6z duyunca a\xE7\u0131klamas\u0131n\u0131 sorard\u0131. \xD6\u011Frenirken herkes anlam\u0131\u015F gibi g\xF6r\xFCnd\xFC\u011F\xFCnde susmak zorunda de\u011Filsin; i\xE7ten bir soru, zihnindeki d\xFC\u011F\xFCm\xFC \xE7\xF6zmek i\xE7in ataca\u011F\u0131n cesur ad\u0131m olabilir.",
      "Aishah would ask for an explanation when she did not understand a saying. Even when everyone else appears to understand, a sincere question can be the courageous step that loosens a knot in your mind.",
      ["courage", "learning", "questions"]
    ),
    c(
      "Asma bint Abi Bakr",
      "Hz. Esm\xE2",
      "bukhari",
      "2979",
      "Esm\xE2, hicret yolculu\u011Funun az\u0131\u011F\u0131n\u0131 ba\u011Flamak i\xE7in ku\u015Fa\u011F\u0131n\u0131 ikiye ay\u0131rd\u0131. Her haz\u0131rl\u0131\u011F\u0131n kusursuz olmas\u0131n\u0131 bekleme; elindeki m\xFCtevaz\u0131 bir imk\xE2n\u0131 dikkatle kullanmak, gerekli bir i\u015Fi bug\xFCn m\xFCmk\xFCn k\u0131labilir.",
      "Asma split her waistband to secure provisions for the migration journey. Preparations need not be perfect; carefully using a modest resource already at hand can make a necessary task possible today.",
      ["courage", "resourcefulness", "action"]
    ),
    c(
      "Asma bint Abi Bakr",
      "Hz. Esm\xE2",
      "bukhari",
      "2620",
      "Esm\xE2, farkl\u0131 inan\xE7taki annesiyle ba\u011F\u0131n\u0131 nas\u0131l s\xFCrd\xFCrece\u011Fini sordu ve g\xF6r\xFC\u015Fmesine izin verildi. Ayr\u0131l\u0131klar ili\u015Fkini zorlad\u0131\u011F\u0131nda ba\u011F\u0131n\u0131 hemen kopmu\u015F sayma; sayg\u0131l\u0131 yak\u0131nl\u0131k kurman\u0131n imk\xE2nlar\u0131n\u0131 ara\u015Ft\u0131rabilirsin.",
      "Asma asked about maintaining ties with her mother of another faith and was permitted to do so. When differences strain a relationship, you can explore respectful closeness before assuming the bond is beyond reach.",
      ["reconciliation", "hope", "family"]
    ),
    c(
      "Umm Salamah",
      "Hz. \xDCmm\xFC Seleme",
      "bukhari",
      "2731",
      "\xDCmm\xFC Seleme, Hudeybiye\u2019de s\xF6zler kar\u015F\u0131l\u0131k bulmay\u0131nca Peygamber\u2019e \xF6nce kendisinin uygulamas\u0131n\u0131 \xF6nerdi. Bazen t\u0131kanan bir i\u015Fi a\xE7an \u015Fey daha \xE7ok konu\u015Fmak de\u011Fil, insanlar\u0131n g\xF6rebilece\u011Fi sakin bir \xF6rnektir.",
      "At Hudaybiyyah, Umm Salamah advised the Prophet to act first when words were not being followed. Sometimes a stalled task opens through a calm example people can see, rather than further speech.",
      ["courage", "leadership", "action"]
    ),
    c(
      "Umm Sulaym",
      "Hz. \xDCmm\xFC S\xFCleym",
      "bukhari",
      "130",
      "\xDCmm\xFC S\xFCleym, mahrem bir konuda \xF6\u011Frenmesi gerekeni \xE7ekincesine ra\u011Fmen sordu. \xD6nemli bir soruyu utand\u0131\u011F\u0131n i\xE7in i\xE7inde b\xFCy\xFCtme; uygun ortam\u0131 ve do\u011Fru ki\u015Fiyi se\xE7erek a\xE7\u0131k\xE7a sorabilirsin.",
      "Umm Sulaym asked what she needed to know about a private matter despite its sensitivity. Do not let embarrassment enlarge an important question inside you; choose the right setting and person, then ask.",
      ["courage", "learning", "honesty"]
    ),
    c(
      "Abu Dharr",
      "Hz. Eb\xFB Zer",
      "bukhari",
      "30",
      "Eb\xFB Zer, birini annesi \xFCzerinden incitti\u011Fi i\xE7in ald\u0131\u011F\u0131 uyar\u0131y\u0131 anlatt\u0131; yan\u0131nda \xE7al\u0131\u015Fanla ayn\u0131 t\xFCr giysiyi payla\u015F\u0131yordu. Ele\u015Ftiriden ka\xE7mak yerine davran\u0131\u015F\u0131n\u0131 d\xFCzeltmen, \xF6zr\xFCne g\xFCnl\xFCk hayatta kar\u015F\u0131l\u0131k verebilir.",
      "Abu Dharr recounted being corrected for insulting someone\u2019s mother; he was seen wearing the same kind of clothes as his servant. Letting criticism change daily conduct can give an apology substance.",
      ["courage", "accountability", "dignity"]
    ),
    c(
      "Anas ibn Malik",
      "Hz. Enes",
      "bukhari",
      "6247",
      "Enes, \xE7ocuklar\u0131n yan\u0131ndan ge\xE7erken onlara selam verdi ve bunu Peygamber\u2019den g\xF6rd\xFC\u011F\xFCn\xFC anlatt\u0131. K\xFC\xE7\xFCk g\xF6rd\xFC\u011F\xFCn bir kar\u015F\u0131la\u015Fma bir \xE7ocu\u011Fa de\u011Ferini hissettirebilir; g\xFCndelik nezaketinde ya\u015Fa g\xF6re kap\u0131lar kapatma.",
      "Anas greeted children he passed, explaining that he had seen the Prophet do so. A seemingly small encounter can help a child feel valued; do not close the doors of everyday courtesy according to age.",
      ["kindness", "dignity", "attention"]
    ),
    c(
      "Abu Hurayrah",
      "Hz. Eb\xFB H\xFCreyre",
      "bukhari",
      "118",
      "Eb\xFB H\xFCreyre, yoksullu\u011Funa ra\u011Fmen \xF6\u011Frenmek i\xE7in Peygamber\u2019in yan\u0131nda ge\xE7irdi\u011Fi zaman\u0131 anlatt\u0131. \u0130mk\xE2nlar\u0131n\u0131n s\u0131n\u0131rl\u0131 olmas\u0131 seni bilgiden d\u0131\u015Flamaz; bug\xFCn eri\u015Febildi\u011Fin bir \xF6\u011Frenme f\u0131rsat\u0131na ger\xE7ekten dikkatini verebilirsin.",
      "Abu Hurayrah described the time he spent learning beside the Prophet despite poverty. Limited resources need not place knowledge beyond you; give genuine attention to a learning opportunity available today.",
      ["hope", "learning", "action"]
    ),
    c(
      "Abdullah ibn Masud",
      "Hz. Abdullah b. Mes\u2018\xFBd",
      "bukhari",
      "70",
      "\u0130bn Mes\u2018\xFBd, daha s\u0131k konu\u015Fmas\u0131 istendi\u011Finde dinleyenlerin usanmas\u0131n\u0131 g\xF6zetti\u011Fini s\xF6yledi. Faydal\u0131 olmak, durmadan anlatmak de\u011Fildir; kar\u015F\u0131ndakinin dikkatini ve yorgunlu\u011Funu hesaba katmak s\xF6z\xFCn\xFC daha \xF6zenli k\u0131lar.",
      "Asked to speak more often, Ibn Masud explained his concern that listeners might become weary. Helping does not require constant explanation; taking another person\u2019s attention and fatigue into account makes speech more considerate.",
      ["care", "teaching", "restraint"]
    ),
    c(
      "Abdullah ibn Masud",
      "Hz. Abdullah b. Mes\u2018\xFBd",
      "bukhari",
      "5002",
      "\u0130bn Mes\u2018\xFBd, Kur\u2019an bilgisinden s\xF6z ederken daha bilgili birine ula\u015Fabilse yolculuk edece\u011Fini s\xF6yledi. \u0130yi bildi\u011Fin bir alanda bile \xF6\u011Frenilecek bir \u015Fey aramak, eme\u011Finin de\u011Ferini azaltmaz.",
      "While describing his knowledge of the Quran, Ibn Masud said he would travel to reach someone who knew more. Looking for something to learn even within your expertise does not diminish the work you have done.",
      ["humility", "learning", "growth"]
    ),
    c(
      "Abdullah ibn Abbas",
      "Hz. Abdullah b. Abb\xE2s",
      "bukhari",
      "4970",
      "\u0130bn Abb\xE2s, ya\u015F\xE7a b\xFCy\xFCklerin bulundu\u011Fu mecliste Nasr s\xFBresinden anlad\u0131\u011F\u0131n\u0131 a\xE7\u0131klad\u0131; \xD6mer de bu anlay\u0131\u015F\u0131 payla\u015Ft\u0131\u011F\u0131n\u0131 s\xF6yledi. Gen\xE7li\u011Fin seni susturmas\u0131n; d\xFC\u015F\xFCnd\xFC\u011F\xFCn\xFC dayana\u011F\u0131yla ve sayg\u0131yla anlatmaya haz\u0131rlan.",
      "In a gathering of elders, Ibn Abbas explained his understanding of Surah Nasr, which Umar shared. Youth need not silence you; prepare to express a considered view respectfully and with its reasons.",
      ["courage", "learning", "voice"]
    ),
    c(
      "Abdullah ibn Abbas",
      "Hz. Abdullah b. Abb\xE2s",
      "bukhari",
      "143",
      "\u0130bn Abb\xE2s, Peygamber i\xE7in abdest suyu haz\u0131rlad\u0131; bu k\xFC\xE7\xFCk hizmeti bir dua izledi. Faydal\u0131 olmak i\xE7in mutlaka b\xFCy\xFCk bir g\xF6rev bekleme; yak\u0131ndaki ger\xE7ek ihtiyac\u0131 fark ederek ba\u015Flayabilirsin.",
      "Ibn Abbas prepared water for the Prophet\u2019s ablution, and this small service was followed by a prayer. You need not await a grand assignment to be useful; begin by noticing a real need nearby.",
      ["service", "initiative", "action"]
    ),
    c(
      "Abdullah ibn Umar",
      "Hz. Abdullah b. \xD6mer",
      "bukhari",
      "1121",
      "\u0130bn \xD6mer, kendisini korkutan r\xFCyay\u0131 i\xE7ine kapatmad\u0131; Hafsa arac\u0131l\u0131\u011F\u0131yla anlatt\u0131 ve namaza y\xF6nelten bir \xF6\u011F\xFCt ald\u0131. Kayg\u0131n\u0131 g\xFCvendi\u011Fin biriyle payla\u015Fmak, ona anlaml\u0131 bir kar\u015F\u0131l\u0131k bulmana yard\u0131mc\u0131 olabilir.",
      "Ibn Umar did not keep a frightening dream locked inside; he shared it through Hafsa and received counsel toward prayer. Speaking with someone trustworthy about anxiety may help you find a meaningful response.",
      ["fear", "support", "devotion"]
    ),
    c(
      "Zayd ibn Thabit",
      "Hz. Zeyd b. S\xE2bit",
      "bukhari",
      "4986",
      "Zeyd, Kur\u2019an\u2019\u0131 toplama sorumlulu\u011Funu bir da\u011F\u0131 ta\u015F\u0131maktan a\u011F\u0131r buldu; ard\u0131ndan titizce ara\u015Ft\u0131rmaya giri\u015Fti. B\xFCy\xFCk bir g\xF6rev g\xF6z\xFCn\xFC korkuttu\u011Funda \xF6nemini ink\xE2r etme; onu dikkatli, denetlenebilir \xE7al\u0131\u015Fmaya b\xF6l.",
      "Zayd felt collecting the Quran would weigh more heavily than moving a mountain, then began painstaking research. When a great responsibility frightens you, acknowledge its weight and divide it into careful, verifiable work.",
      ["fear", "courage", "responsibility"]
    ),
    c(
      "Kaab ibn Malik",
      "Hz. K\xE2\u2018b b. M\xE2lik",
      "bukhari",
      "4418",
      "K\xE2\u2018b, Teb\xFCk\u2019e kat\u0131lmamas\u0131n\u0131 a\xE7\u0131klarken bir mazeret uydurmak yerine ger\xE7e\u011Fi s\xF6yledi ve zor sonu\xE7larla y\xFCzle\u015Fti. Hatan\u0131 kabul etmek korkutabilir; d\xFCr\xFCst\xE7e sorumluluk almak, onarmaya ba\u015Flayaca\u011F\u0131n sa\u011Flam bir zemin olabilir.",
      "Explaining his absence from Tabuk, Kaab chose truth over an invented excuse and faced difficult consequences. Admitting a mistake can be frightening; honest responsibility can provide firm ground from which to begin repair.",
      ["fear", "courage", "honesty"]
    ),
    c(
      "Abd al-Rahman ibn Awf",
      "Hz. Abdurrahman b. Avf",
      "bukhari",
      "2049",
      "Abdurrahman, Medine\u2019de kendisine yard\u0131m sunan dostuna dua etti ve pazar\u0131n yolunu sordu. Yeni bir yerde \xE7ekinsen de yol sorabilirsin; destekle kendi eme\u011Fin aras\u0131nda verimli bir ba\u011F kurabilirsin.",
      "In Medina, Abd al-Rahman blessed the friend offering help and asked the way to the market. Even when a new place feels intimidating, you can ask directions and connect support with your own effort.",
      ["courage", "work", "initiative"]
    ),
    c(
      "Hanzalah",
      "Hz. Hanzala",
      "muslim",
      "2750a",
      "Hanzala, manev\xEE h\xE2li de\u011Fi\u015Fti\u011Finde kendinden korktu; Eb\xFB Bekir\u2019le konu\u015Fup Peygamber\u2019e sordu. Hislerinin her an ayn\u0131 olmamas\u0131 seni sahte yapmaz; kayg\u0131n\u0131 a\xE7\u0131k\xE7a konu\u015Farak daha dengeli bir anlay\u0131\u015F arayabilirsin.",
      "Hanzalah feared for himself when his spiritual feelings changed; he spoke with Abu Bakr and asked the Prophet. Feelings need not remain constant for sincerity to be real; discuss the worry and seek a more balanced understanding.",
      ["fear", "reassurance", "balance"]
    ),
    h2(
      "translation",
      "bukhari",
      "5641",
      "Bir M\xFCsl\xFCmana dokunan yorgunluk, hastal\u0131k, kayg\u0131, h\xFCz\xFCn, incinme veya keder yoktur ki, aya\u011F\u0131na batan bir diken bile olsa, Allah bununla onun hatalar\u0131ndan bir k\u0131sm\u0131n\u0131 silmesin.",
      "No fatigue, illness, anxiety, sadness, hurt, or distress touches a Muslim, even a thorn\u2019s prick, without God erasing some of that person\u2019s faults through it.",
      ["fear", "suffering", "hope"]
    ),
    h2(
      "translation",
      "muslim",
      "2999",
      "M\xFCminin durumu ne hayret vericidir; onun her h\xE2li hay\u0131rd\u0131r. Bu yaln\u0131z m\xFCmine \xF6zg\xFCd\xFCr: Sevindirici bir \u015Fey ya\u015Farsa \u015F\xFCkreder, bu ona hay\u0131r olur; s\u0131k\u0131nt\u0131 ya\u015Farsa sabreder, bu da ona hay\u0131r olur.",
      "How remarkable is a believer\u2019s condition: every circumstance offers good, something particular to the believer. In happiness there is gratitude and good; in hardship there is patience and good.",
      ["hope", "gratitude", "patience"]
    ),
    h2(
      "adaptation",
      "bukhari",
      "7405",
      "Allah\u2019\u0131 anarken zihnini yaln\u0131zca reddedilme korkusuyla doldurma. Bu kuds\xEE hadis, kulun y\xF6neli\u015Fine yak\u0131nl\u0131kla kar\u015F\u0131l\u0131k verilmesini anlat\u0131r; duaya ba\u015Flarken rahmeti de d\xFC\u015F\xFCnmene, g\xFCvenle yeniden y\xF6nelmene yer vard\u0131r.",
      "Do not fill remembrance of God only with fear of rejection. This sacred report describes closeness meeting a servant\u2019s approach; there is room to think of mercy as you begin praying and turn back with trust.",
      ["fear", "hope", "remembrance"]
    ),
    h2(
      "adaptation",
      "muslim",
      "2747a",
      "Hadiste t\xF6vbenin sevinci, \xE7\xF6lde kaybetti\u011Fi bine\u011Fini yeniden bulan insan\u0131n sevincinden daha b\xFCy\xFCk anlat\u0131l\u0131r. D\xF6n\xFC\u015F\xFCn\xFC yaln\u0131z utan\xE7la d\xFC\u015F\xFCnme; yanl\u0131\u015F\u0131n\u0131 b\u0131rak\u0131p yeniden y\xF6nelmende umut ta\u015F\u0131yan bir kar\u015F\u0131lan\u0131\u015F vard\u0131r.",
      "The report portrays joy at repentance as greater than the joy of recovering a lost mount in the desert. Let returning mean more than shame: turning away from wrong carries the hope of welcome.",
      ["hope", "repentance", "courage"]
    ),
    h2(
      "adaptation",
      "bukhari",
      "6463",
      "Peygamber, kendisinin de Allah\u2019\u0131n rahmetine muhta\xE7 oldu\u011Funu s\xF6yledi. Her \u015Feyi kusursuz yapamazsan de\u011Fersiz olaca\u011F\u0131n korkusunu gev\u015Fet; \xF6l\xE7\xFCl\xFC eme\u011Fini s\xFCrd\xFCr\xFCrken rahmete muhta\xE7 olman\u0131n insanl\u0131\u011F\u0131n\u0131 eksiltmedi\u011Fini hat\u0131rla.",
      "The Prophet said that he too depended on God\u2019s mercy. Loosen the fear that imperfection makes you worthless; keep making measured efforts while remembering that needing mercy does not diminish your humanity.",
      ["fear", "mercy", "balance"]
    ),
    h2(
      "adaptation",
      "bukhari",
      "6491",
      "Bu hadis, hen\xFCz ger\xE7ekle\u015Ftiremedi\u011Fin iyi niyetin de hesaba kat\u0131ld\u0131\u011F\u0131n\u0131 anlat\u0131r. Elinden gelmeyen bir sonuca \xFCz\xFCl\xFCrken i\xE7indeki iyilik iste\u011Fini silme; yapabildi\u011Fin zaman onu davran\u0131\u015Fa ta\u015F\u0131maya haz\u0131r tut.",
      "This report gives weight even to a good intention not yet carried out. When an outcome lies beyond you, do not erase your desire for good; keep it ready to become action when you can.",
      ["hope", "intention", "action"]
    ),
    h2(
      "adaptation",
      "muslim",
      "91a",
      "G\xFCzel giyinmekle kibir ayn\u0131 \u015Fey de\u011Fildir; hadiste kibir, ger\xE7e\u011Fi reddetmek ve insanlar\u0131 k\xFC\xE7\xFCmsemekle a\xE7\u0131klan\u0131r. Kendine \xF6zen g\xF6sterirken ba\u015Fkas\u0131n\u0131n de\u011Ferini azaltmadan da g\xFCvenle var olabilirsin.",
      "Dressing well and arrogance are not the same; the report explains arrogance as refusing truth and looking down on people. You can take care of yourself and stand confidently without lowering another person\u2019s worth.",
      ["confidence", "humility", "dignity"]
    ),
    h2(
      "adaptation",
      "muslim",
      "2567a",
      "Bir dostunu yaln\u0131z Allah i\xE7in sevdi\u011Finden ziyaret eden ki\u015Fi hadiste \xF6v\xFCl\xFCr. \u0130li\u015Fkilerini s\xFCrekli kar\u015F\u0131l\u0131k hesab\u0131na s\u0131k\u0131\u015Ft\u0131rma; bug\xFCn birini \xE7\u0131kar beklemeden aramak, sevgini ger\xE7ek bir kar\u015F\u0131la\u015Fmaya d\xF6n\xFC\u015Ft\xFCrebilir.",
      "The report honors someone visiting a friend solely out of love for God. Let relationships extend beyond calculations of return; contacting someone without seeking advantage can give affection a real encounter.",
      ["friendship", "sincerity", "action"]
    ),
    h2(
      "translation",
      "bukhari",
      "5534",
      "\u0130yi arkada\u015F ile k\xF6t\xFC arkada\u015F\u0131n \xF6rne\u011Fi, misk ta\u015F\u0131yanla k\xF6r\xFCk \xFCfleyen gibidir. Misk ta\u015F\u0131yan ya sana bir miktar verir, ya ondan sat\u0131n al\u0131rs\u0131n yahut yan\u0131nda g\xFCzel bir koku bulursun.",
      "A good companion and a bad one resemble a musk bearer and a bellows blower. The musk bearer may give you some, you may buy from him, or you may enjoy a pleasant fragrance beside him.",
      ["friendship", "discernment", "influence"],
      true
    ),
    h2(
      "translation",
      "muslim",
      "2674",
      "Kim do\u011Fru yola \xE7a\u011F\u0131r\u0131rsa, kendisine uyanlar\u0131n \xF6d\xFClleri kadar ona da \xF6d\xFCl vard\u0131r; bu, onlar\u0131n \xF6d\xFCllerinden hi\xE7bir \u015Feyi eksiltmez. K\xF6t\xFC yola \xE7a\u011F\u0131ran ise uyanlar\u0131n g\xFCnahlar\u0131 kadar y\xFCk ta\u015F\u0131r.",
      "Whoever calls toward guidance receives a reward like those who follow, without their rewards being reduced. Whoever calls toward error bears a burden like the sins of those who follow.",
      ["responsibility", "influence", "action"],
      true
    ),
    h2(
      "adaptation",
      "bukhari",
      "6126",
      "\xC2i\u015Fe, Peygamber\u2019in g\xFCnah olmayan iki se\xE7enekten kolay olan\u0131n\u0131 se\xE7ti\u011Fini anlatt\u0131. Bir i\u015Fin de\u011Ferini \xE7ekti\u011Fin zorlukla \xF6l\xE7mek zorunda de\u011Filsin; do\u011Fru ve kolay yol \xF6n\xFCndeyse onu g\xF6n\xFCl rahatl\u0131\u011F\u0131yla kullanabilirsin.",
      "Aishah reported that the Prophet chose the easier of two options when no sin was involved. Difficulty need not measure a task\u2019s worth; if a sound, easier way is open, you can take it with a clear conscience.",
      ["ease", "confidence", "discernment"],
      false,
      true
    ),
    h2(
      "adaptation",
      "bukhari",
      "6133",
      "M\xFCminin ayn\u0131 delikten iki kez \u0131s\u0131r\u0131lmamas\u0131 \xF6\u011F\xFCd\xFC, ya\u015Fad\u0131\u011F\u0131ndan \xF6\u011Frenmeye \xE7a\u011F\u0131r\u0131r. Yeniden denemek istiyorsan \xF6nce incindi\u011Fin noktay\u0131 incele; cesaretine yeni bir tedbir eklemek, umudunu daha dikkatli ta\u015F\u0131r.",
      "The counsel against being bitten twice from the same hole invites learning from experience. Before trying again, examine where you were hurt; adding a new precaution lets you carry hope more carefully.",
      ["courage", "prudence", "learning"]
    ),
    h2(
      "translation",
      "muslim",
      "2607c",
      "Do\u011Fruluk iyili\u011Fe g\xF6t\xFCr\xFCr, iyilik de cennete g\xF6t\xFCr\xFCr. \u0130nsan do\u011Fru s\xF6ylemeye ve do\u011Frulu\u011Fu aramaya devam eder; sonunda Allah kat\u0131nda dosdo\u011Fru biri olarak kayda ge\xE7irilir.",
      "Truthfulness leads toward goodness, and goodness toward Paradise. A person continues speaking truth and pursuing honesty until being recorded before God as someone deeply truthful.",
      ["honesty", "steadiness", "integrity"],
      true
    ),
    h2(
      "adaptation",
      "bukhari",
      "2076",
      "Satarken, al\u0131rken ve hakk\u0131n\u0131 isterken kolayl\u0131k g\xF6sterene rahmet dilenir. Hakk\u0131n\u0131 savunmak i\xE7in sesini sertle\u015Ftirmen gerekmeyebilir; bug\xFCnk\xFC bir al\u0131\u015Fveri\u015Fte veya talepte a\xE7\u0131kl\u0131kla nezaketi yan yana tut.",
      "Mercy is sought for the person who is considerate when selling, buying, or requesting what is due. Assertiveness need not require harshness; combine clarity and courtesy in a transaction or request today.",
      ["kindness", "fairness", "confidence"]
    ),
    h2(
      "translation",
      "bukhari",
      "2072",
      "Hi\xE7 kimse kendi ellerinin eme\u011Finden yedi\u011Fi yiyecekten daha hay\u0131rl\u0131s\u0131n\u0131 yememi\u015Ftir. Allah\u2019\u0131n peygamberi D\xE2v\xFBd da ge\xE7imini kendi elleriyle yapt\u0131\u011F\u0131 i\u015Fin kazanc\u0131ndan sa\u011Fl\u0131yor, ondan yiyordu.",
      "No one has eaten food better than what their own hands have earned. David, God\u2019s prophet, likewise ate from the earnings of his own work.",
      ["work", "dignity", "effort"]
    ),
    h2(
      "translation",
      "bukhari",
      "2320",
      "Bir M\xFCsl\xFCman bir a\u011Fa\xE7 diker veya ekin eker de ondan bir ku\u015F, bir insan yahut bir hayvan yerse, bu onun i\xE7in sadaka say\u0131l\u0131r.",
      "When a Muslim plants a tree or sows a crop, whatever a bird, person, or animal eats from it is counted as charity for the planter.",
      ["work", "nature", "generosity"]
    ),
    h2(
      "translation",
      "bukhari",
      "5460",
      "Birinizin hizmetlisi yeme\u011Fini getirdi\u011Finde, onu yan\u0131na oturtmayacaksa kendisine bir iki lokma yahut yemekten k\xFC\xE7\xFCk bir pay versin; \xE7\xFCnk\xFC yeme\u011Fin s\u0131cakl\u0131\u011F\u0131n\u0131 ve haz\u0131rlama zahmetini o \xE7ekmi\u015Ftir.",
      "When your servant brings your meal, if you do not seat them beside you, give them a bite or two, or a little food; they endured its heat and the work of preparing it.",
      ["gratitude", "dignity", "labor"]
    ),
    h2(
      "adaptation",
      "muslim",
      "2626",
      "Birini g\xFCler y\xFCzle kar\u015F\u0131lamak bile k\xFC\xE7\xFCmsenmeyecek bir iyilik olarak an\u0131l\u0131r. Her kar\u015F\u0131la\u015Fmada etkileyici s\xF6zler bulmaya \xE7al\u0131\u015Fma; y\xFCz\xFCndeki a\xE7\u0131kl\u0131k ve s\u0131cakl\u0131k, kar\u015F\u0131ndakine bug\xFCn yakla\u015F\u0131labilir bir yer sunabilir.",
      "Meeting someone with a cheerful face is named as goodness that should not be dismissed. You need not find impressive words for every encounter; an open, warm expression can offer an approachable place today.",
      ["kindness", "connection", "ease"]
    ),
    h2(
      "adaptation",
      "muslim",
      "2625a",
      "\xC7orba pi\u015Firirken suyunu art\u0131r\u0131p kom\u015Fuyu g\xF6zetme \xF6\u011F\xFCd\xFC, payla\u015Fmay\u0131 g\xFCndelik mutfa\u011Fa ta\u015F\u0131r. Vermek i\xE7in kusursuz bir sofra bekleme; elindekinden ay\u0131rabilece\u011Fin bir porsiyonla yak\u0131n\u0131ndaki ihtiyac\u0131 fark edebilirsin.",
      "The counsel to add water to broth and remember neighbors brings sharing into an ordinary kitchen. Giving need not await a perfect table; a portion you can spare can answer a nearby need.",
      ["generosity", "neighbors", "action"]
    ),
    h2(
      "adaptation",
      "bukhari",
      "6000",
      "Yavrusuna basmamak i\xE7in aya\u011F\u0131n\u0131 kald\u0131ran hayvan bile hadiste yery\xFCz\xFCndeki merhametin \xF6rne\u011Fidir. G\xFCc\xFCn\xFC yaln\u0131z yapabildiklerinle \xF6l\xE7me; zarar vermemek i\xE7in kendini tuttu\u011Fun anlarda da \u015Fefkatin g\xF6r\xFCn\xFCr olabilir.",
      "Even an animal lifting its hoof to avoid its young appears as an image of mercy on earth. Strength can show not only in what you do, but in the restraint that prevents harm.",
      ["mercy", "restraint", "care"]
    ),
    h2(
      "adaptation",
      "bukhari",
      "5999",
      "Peygamber, \xE7ocu\u011Funa kavu\u015Fup onu ba\u011Fr\u0131na basan anneyi g\xF6stererek Allah\u2019\u0131n merhametinin daha b\xFCy\xFCk oldu\u011Funu anlatt\u0131. \u0130\xE7ini terk edilme korkusu kaplad\u0131\u011F\u0131nda, rahmeti de d\xFC\u015F\xFCncene davet edebilece\u011Fini hat\u0131rla.",
      "Pointing to a mother holding the child she had found, the Prophet described God\u2019s mercy as greater still. When fear of abandonment fills you, remember that mercy can also be invited into your thoughts.",
      ["fear", "hope", "mercy"]
    ),
    h2(
      "adaptation",
      "bukhari",
      "5997",
      "Peygamber\u2019in torununu \xF6pmesi, \u015Fefkati g\xF6stermeye uzak duran birine merhameti hat\u0131rlatt\u0131. Sevgini yaln\u0131zca i\xE7inde ta\u015F\u0131ma; uygun bir sar\u0131lma veya yak\u0131nl\u0131kla sevdi\u011Fine onun i\xE7in orada oldu\u011Funu hissettirebilirsin.",
      "The Prophet\u2019s kiss for his grandson prompted a reminder about mercy to someone unused to showing affection. Let love move beyond the inward: fitting closeness can help a loved one feel your presence.",
      ["affection", "mercy", "family"],
      false,
      true
    ),
    h2(
      "adaptation",
      "bukhari",
      "6203",
      "Peygamber, k\xFC\xE7\xFCk Eb\xFB Umeyr\u2019e ku\u015Funu sorarak onun d\xFCnyas\u0131na ilgi g\xF6sterirdi. Sana \xF6nemsiz g\xF6r\xFCnen \u015Fey ba\u015Fkas\u0131 i\xE7in b\xFCy\xFCk olabilir; sevdi\u011Finin anlatt\u0131\u011F\u0131 ayr\u0131nt\u0131ya bug\xFCn ger\xE7ekten kulak ver.",
      "The Prophet asked little Abu Umayr about his bird, taking an interest in his world. What seems minor to you may matter greatly to someone else; truly listen to a detail a loved one shares today.",
      ["attention", "empathy", "listening"],
      false,
      true
    ),
    h2(
      "adaptation",
      "bukhari",
      "5649",
      "A\xE7lar\u0131 doyurmak, hastalar\u0131 ziyaret etmek ve esirlerin \xF6zg\xFCrl\xFC\u011F\xFCne yard\u0131m etmek birlikte \xF6\u011F\xFCtlenir. Merhametine bir adres bul; birinin ihtiyac\u0131n\u0131 kar\u015F\u0131lamak, yaln\u0131zl\u0131\u011F\u0131n\u0131 payla\u015Fmak veya \xF6zg\xFCrl\xFC\u011F\xFCn\xFC desteklemek i\xE7in sorumluluk al.",
      "Feeding the hungry, visiting the sick, and helping captives regain freedom are urged together. Give compassion a destination: take responsibility for someone\u2019s need, loneliness, or freedom.",
      ["service", "compassion", "responsibility"]
    ),
    h2(
      "translation",
      "muslim",
      "1631",
      "\u0130nsan \xF6ld\xFC\u011F\xFCnde ameli kesilir; \xFC\xE7 \u015Fey bunun d\u0131\u015F\u0131ndad\u0131r: Faydas\u0131 s\xFCren bir sadaka, insanlar\u0131n yararland\u0131\u011F\u0131 bilgi ve arkas\u0131ndan kendisi i\xE7in dua eden hay\u0131rl\u0131 bir evlat.",
      "When a person dies, their deeds cease except in three ways: charity whose benefit continues, knowledge people use, and a righteous child who prays for them.",
      ["legacy", "knowledge", "generosity"]
    ),
    h2(
      "adaptation",
      "bukhari",
      "1427",
      "Vermeye ba\u015Flarken sorumlulu\u011Fundaki insanlar\u0131 g\xF6zetme \xF6\u011F\xFCd\xFC de vard\u0131r. C\xF6mertli\u011Fini ba\u015Fkalar\u0131na yeti\u015Firken evindekileri unutaca\u011F\u0131n bir yar\u0131\u015Fa \xE7evirme; \xF6nce \xFCstlendi\u011Fin ihtiya\xE7lar\u0131 g\xF6r, payla\u015F\u0131m\u0131n\u0131 bu \xF6zenin \xFCzerine kur.",
      "The counsel about giving also asks us to begin with those in our care. Let generosity include your household\u2019s needs rather than become a race past them; build sharing upon responsibility.",
      ["responsibility", "family", "generosity"]
    ),
    h2(
      "adaptation",
      "muslim",
      "1829a",
      "Hepimizin bir emanetin g\xF6zeticisi oldu\u011Funu hat\u0131rlatan hadis, sorumlulu\u011Fu yaln\u0131z y\xF6neticilere b\u0131rakmaz. Bug\xFCn etki alan\u0131na bak; bak\u0131m\u0131n\u0131, g\xFCvenini veya i\u015Fini \xFCstlendi\u011Fin biri i\xE7in yerine getirmen gerekeni se\xE7.",
      "The report reminding us that each person is a guardian does not reserve responsibility for leaders. Look at your sphere of influence and choose what you owe someone whose care, trust, or work is entrusted to you.",
      ["responsibility", "trust", "action"]
    ),
    h2(
      "adaptation",
      "muslim",
      "55a",
      "Dinin nasihat ve i\xE7ten ba\u011Fl\u0131l\u0131kla anlat\u0131lmas\u0131, inanc\u0131 ili\u015Fkilerde de d\xFCr\xFCst\xE7e ya\u015Famaya \xE7a\u011F\u0131r\u0131r. \u0130yi g\xF6r\xFCnmenin \xF6tesine ge\xE7; bug\xFCn birine verdi\u011Fin \xF6\u011F\xFCtte onun ger\xE7ek yarar\u0131n\u0131 ne kadar g\xF6zetti\u011Fini d\xFC\u015F\xFCn.",
      "Describing religion through sincere counsel and commitment calls for honesty in relationships too. Look beyond appearing good and consider how carefully today\u2019s advice serves another person\u2019s real welfare.",
      ["sincerity", "integrity", "care"]
    ),
    h2(
      "adaptation",
      "muslim",
      "2721a",
      "Peygamber\u2019in duas\u0131nda do\u011Fru y\xF6n, sorumluluk bilinci, iffet ve g\xF6n\xFCl yeterlili\u011Fi istenir. \u0130steklerini s\u0131ralarken nas\u0131l bir insan olmak istedi\u011Fini de d\xFC\u015F\xFCn; duan karakterin i\xE7in bir y\xF6n belirleyebilir.",
      "The Prophet\u2019s prayer asks for guidance, mindfulness, chastity, and sufficiency. Alongside listing what you want, consider the person you wish to become; prayer can give your character a direction.",
      ["prayer", "character", "direction"]
    ),
    h2(
      "adaptation",
      "bukhari",
      "6340",
      "Dua ettim ama kar\u015F\u0131l\u0131k bulmad\u0131m diyerek aceleye kap\u0131lmamak \xF6\u011F\xFCtlenir. Bekleyi\u015Fin zor geldi\u011Finde bunu kendine kar\u015F\u0131 bir h\xFCkme d\xF6n\xFC\u015Ft\xFCrme; niyaz\u0131n\u0131 s\xFCrd\xFCr\xFCrken zaman\u0131n\u0131 yaln\u0131zca sonu\xE7 sayarak t\xFCketmek zorunda de\u011Filsin.",
      "The counsel warns against becoming impatient and declaring prayer unanswered. When waiting is difficult, do not turn it into a verdict against yourself; continuing to pray need not mean measuring every moment by results.",
      ["uncertainty", "patience", "hope"]
    )
  ];
  var FAITH_QUOTES_MORE = drafts2.map((entry, index) => ({
    id: `faith-more-${String(index + 1).padStart(3, "0")}`,
    ...entry
  }));

  // src/data/quoteExpansionScienceMore.ts
